#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:592
msgid "abc"
msgstr "abc"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:594
msgid ""
"New function :func:`abc.get_cache_token` can be used to know when to "
"invalidate caches that are affected by changes in the object graph.  "
"(Contributed by Łukasz Langa in :issue:`16832`.)"
msgstr ""
"Nová funkce :func:`abc.get_cache_token` lze použít k známému kdy obnovit "
"cache, které jsou ovlivňovany změnami v grafu objektů. (Přispěl Łukasz Langa"
" v :issue:`16832`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:598
msgid ""
"New class :class:`~abc.ABC` has :class:`~abc.ABCMeta` as its meta class. "
"Using ``ABC`` as a base class has essentially the same effect as specifying "
"``metaclass=abc.ABCMeta``, but is simpler to type and easier to read. "
"(Contributed by Bruno Dupuis in :issue:`16049`.)"
msgstr ""
"Nová třída :class:`~abc.ABC` má :class:`~abc.ABCMeta` jako svůj meta třídu. "
"Použití ``ABC`` jako základní třídy má v podstatě stejný efekt jako zadání "
"``metaclass=abc.ABCMeta``, ale je jednodušší na psání a lépe se čte. "
"(Přispěl Bruno Dupuis v :issue:`16049`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:605
msgid "aifc"
msgstr "aifc"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:607
msgid ""
"The :meth:`!getparams` method now returns a namedtuple rather than a plain "
"tuple.  (Contributed by Claudiu Popa in :issue:`17818`.)"
msgstr ""
"Metoda :meth:`!getparams` nyní vrací pojmenovanétuple místo občejného tuple."
" (Přispěl Claudiu Popa v :issue:`17818`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:610
msgid ""
":func:`!aifc.open` now supports the context management protocol: when used "
"in a :keyword:`with` block, the :meth:`!close` method of the returned object"
" will be called automatically at the end of the block.  (Contributed by "
"Serhiy Storchacha in :issue:`16486`.)"
msgstr ""
":func:`!aifc.open` nyní podporuje protokol správy kontextu: je-li použito v "
":keyword:`with` bloku, bude metoda :meth:`!close` vráceného objektu volána "
"automaticky na konci bloku. (Přispěl Serhiy Storchacha v :issue:`16486`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:615 ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1543
msgid ""
"The :meth:`!writeframesraw` and :meth:`!writeframes` methods now accept any "
":term:`bytes-like object`.  (Contributed by Serhiy Storchaka in "
":issue:`8311`.)"
msgstr ""
"Metody :meth:`!writeframesraw` a :meth:`!writeframes` nyní přijíjmají "
"libovolný :term:`bytes-like object`. (Přispěl Serhiy Storchaka v "
":issue:`8311`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:621
msgid "argparse"
msgstr "argparse"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:623
msgid ""
"The :class:`~argparse.FileType` class now accepts *encoding* and *errors* "
"arguments, which are passed through to :func:`open`.  (Contributed by Lucas "
"Maystre in :issue:`11175`.)"
msgstr ""
"Třída :class:`~argparse.FileType` nyní přijíjmá argumenty *encoding* a "
"*errors*, které jsou předány :func:`open`. (Přispěl Lucas Maystre v "
":issue:`11175`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:629
msgid "audioop"
msgstr "audioop"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:631
msgid ""
":mod:`!audioop` now supports 24-bit samples.  (Contributed by Serhiy "
"Storchaka in :issue:`12866`.)"
msgstr ""
":mod:`!audioop` nyní podporuje 24-bitové vzorky. (Přispěl Serhiy Storchaka v"
" :issue:`12866`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:634
msgid ""
"New :func:`!byteswap` function converts big-endian samples to little-endian "
"and vice versa.  (Contributed by Serhiy Storchaka in :issue:`19641`.)"
msgstr ""
"Nová funkce :func:`!byteswap` konvertuje big-endian vzorky na little-endian "
"a naopak. (Přispěl Serhiy Storchaka v :issue:`19641`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:638
msgid ""
"All :mod:`!audioop` functions now accept any :term:`bytes-like object`.  "
"Strings are not accepted: they didn't work before, now they raise an error "
"right away. (Contributed by Serhiy Storchaka in :issue:`16685`.)"
msgstr ""
"Všechny funkce :mod:`!audioop` nyní přijíjmají jakýkoli :term:`bytes-like "
"object`. Řetězce nejsou přijaté: dříve nefungovaly, nyní okamžitě vyvolávají"
" chybu. (Přispěl Serhiy Storchaka v :issue:`16685`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:644
msgid "base64"
msgstr "base64"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:646
msgid ""
"The encoding and decoding functions in :mod:`base64` now accept any "
":term:`bytes-like object` in cases where it previously required a "
":class:`bytes` or :class:`bytearray` instance.  (Contributed by Nick Coghlan"
" in :issue:`17839`.)"
msgstr ""
"Funkce kódování a dékódování v :mod:`base64` nyní přijíjmají jakýkoli "
":term:`bytes-like object` v případech, kde dříve vyžadovaly instanci "
":class:`bytes` nebo :class:`bytearray`. (Přispěl Nick Coghlan v "
":issue:`17839`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:651
msgid ""
"New functions :func:`~base64.a85encode`, :func:`~base64.a85decode`, "
":func:`~base64.b85encode`, and :func:`~base64.b85decode` provide the ability"
" to encode and decode binary data from and to ``Ascii85`` and the "
"git/mercurial ``Base85`` formats, respectively.  The ``a85`` functions have "
"options that can be used to make them compatible with the variants of the "
"``Ascii85`` encoding, including the Adobe variant.  (Contributed by Martin "
"Morrison, the Mercurial project, Serhiy Storchaka, and Antoine Pitrou in "
":issue:`17618`.)"
msgstr ""
"Nové funkce :func:`~base64.a85encode`, :func:`~base64.a85decode`, "
":func:`~base64.b85encode` a :func:`~base64.b85decode` poskytují schopnost "
"kódovat a dékódovat binární data z formátů ``Ascii85`` a git/mercurial "
"``Base85`` a obráceně. Funkce ``a85`` mají volby, které je lze použít k "
"tomu, aby byly kompatibilní s variantami kódování ``Ascii85``, včetně "
"varianty Adobe. (Přispěli Martin Morrison, projekt Mercurial, Serhiy "
"Storchaka a Antoine Pitrou v :issue:`17618`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:661
msgid "collections"
msgstr "collections"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:663
msgid ""
"The :meth:`.ChainMap.new_child` method now accepts an *m* argument "
"specifying the child map to add to the chain.  This allows an existing "
"mapping and/or a custom mapping type to be used for the child.  (Contributed"
" by Vinay Sajip in :issue:`16613`.)"
msgstr ""
"Metoda :meth:`.ChainMap.new_child` nyní přijíjmá argument *m* určující mapu "
"dítete, kterou chcete přidat do řetězce. To umožnňuje použítí existujícího "
"mapování a/nebo vlastního typu mapování pro dítě. (Přispěl Vinay Sajip v "
":issue:`16613`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:670
msgid "colorsys"
msgstr "colorsys"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:672
msgid ""
"The number of digits in the coefficients for the RGB --- YIQ conversions "
"have been expanded so that they match the FCC NTSC versions.  The change in "
"results should be less than 1% and may better match results found elsewhere."
" (Contributed by Brian Landers and Serhiy Storchaka in :issue:`14323`.)"
msgstr ""
"Počet čísel v koeficientech pro konverze RGB --- YIQ byla rozšířena tak, aby"
" odpovïdaly verzím FCC NTSC. Změna výsledků by měla být méně než 1 % a může "
"lépe shodovat výsledky nalezené jinde. (Přispěli Brian Landers a Serhiy "
"Storchaka v :issue:`14323`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:679
msgid "contextlib"
msgstr "contextlib"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:681
msgid ""
"The new :class:`contextlib.suppress` context manager helps to clarify the "
"intent of code that deliberately suppresses exceptions from a single "
"statement.  (Contributed by Raymond Hettinger in :issue:`15806` and Zero "
"Piraeus in :issue:`19266`.)"
msgstr ""
"Nová kontextní správce :class:`contextlib.suppress` pomáhá objasnit záměr "
"kódu, který záměrně potlačuje výíjimky z jedné příkazy. (Přispěl Raymond "
"Hettinger v :issue:`15806` a Zero Piraeus v :issue:`19266`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:686
msgid ""
"The new :func:`contextlib.redirect_stdout` context manager makes it easier "
"for utility scripts to handle inflexible APIs that write their output to "
":data:`sys.stdout` and don't provide any options to redirect it.  Using the "
"context manager, the :data:`sys.stdout` output can be redirected to any "
"other stream or, in conjunction with :class:`io.StringIO`, to a string. The "
"latter can be especially useful, for example, to capture output from a "
"function that was written to implement a command line interface. It is "
"recommended only for utility scripts because it affects the global state of "
":data:`sys.stdout`.  (Contributed by Raymond Hettinger in :issue:`15805`.)"
msgstr ""
"Nová kontextní správce :func:`contextlib.redirect_stdout` usnadnňuje "
"utilíním skriptům zacházet s rigidly API, který čísu svůj výstup na "
":data:`sys.stdout` a neposkytuje žádné možnosti pro jeho přesměrování. "
"Pomocí kontextní správce lze výstup :data:`sys.stdout` přesměrovat na "
"jakýkoli jiný proud nebo, v kombinaci s :class:`io.StringIO`, na řetězec. "
"Poslední jmenované může být obzvláště užitečné, například na záchytu výstupu"
" z funkce, která byla napsána k implementaci rozhraní příkazového řádku. "
"Doporučuje se pouze pro umnę užívají skripty, protože ovlivňuje globální "
"stav :data:`sys.stdout`. (Přispěl Raymond Hettinger v :issue:`15805`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:697
msgid ""
"The :mod:`contextlib` documentation has also been updated to include a "
":ref:`discussion <single-use-reusable-and-reentrant-cms>` of the differences"
" between single use, reusable and reentrant context managers."
msgstr ""
"Dokumentace :mod:`contextlib` byla také aktualizována tak, aby zahrnovala "
":ref:`diskuzi <single-use-reusable-and-reentrant-cms>` rozdílů mezi "
"jednopoužitelnými, znovupoužitelnými a re-vstupitelnými kontextními správci."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:703
msgid "dbm"
msgstr "dbm"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:705
msgid ""
":func:`dbm.open` objects now support the context management protocol.  When "
"used in a :keyword:`with` statement, the ``close`` method of the database "
"object will be called automatically at the end of the block.  (Contributed "
"by Claudiu Popa and Nick Coghlan in :issue:`19282`.)"
msgstr ""
"Objekty :func:`dbm.open` nyní podporují protokol správy kontextu. Pokud je "
"použito v příkazu :keyword:`with`, bude metoda ``close`` objektu databáze "
"volána automaticky na konci bloku. (Přispěli Claudiu Popa a Nick Coghlan v "
":issue:`19282`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:712
msgid "dis"
msgstr "dis"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:714
msgid ""
"Functions :func:`~dis.show_code`, :func:`~dis.dis`, :func:`~dis.distb`, and "
":func:`~dis.disassemble` now accept a keyword-only *file* argument that "
"controls where they write their output."
msgstr ""
"Funkce :func:`~dis.show_code`, :func:`~dis.dis`, :func:`~dis.distb` a "
":func:`~dis.disassemble` nyní přijíjmají argument :code:`*file*` pouze s "
"klíčem, který kontroluje, kam psí svýstup."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:718
msgid ""
"The :mod:`dis` module is now built around an :class:`~dis.Instruction` class"
" that provides object oriented access to the details of each individual "
"bytecode operation."
msgstr ""
"Modul :mod:`dis` je nyní zabudován okolo třídy :class:`~dis.Instruction`, "
"která poskytuje objektově orientovaný přístup k detailům každé jednotlivé "
"operace bytecode."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:722
msgid ""
"A new method, :func:`~dis.get_instructions`, provides an iterator that emits"
" the Instruction stream for a given piece of Python code.  Thus it is now "
"possible to write a program that inspects and manipulates a bytecode object "
"in ways different from those provided by the :mod:`~dis` module itself.  For"
" example::"
msgstr ""
"Nová metoda :func:`~dis.get_instructions` poskytuje itertor, který emituje "
"proud Instruction pro daný ýsek kódu Python. Je tedy nyní možné napsat "
"program, který inspektor a manipuluje bytecode objekt způsoby odlišné od "
"těch, které poskytuje modul :mod:`~dis` sám. Například::"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:728
msgid ""
">>> import dis\n"
">>> for instr in dis.get_instructions(lambda x: x + 1):\n"
"...     print(instr.opname)\n"
"LOAD_FAST\n"
"LOAD_CONST\n"
"BINARY_ADD\n"
"RETURN_VALUE"
msgstr ""
">>> import dis\n"
">>> for instr in dis.get_instructions(lambda x: x + 1):\n"
"...     print(instr.opname)\n"
"LOAD_FAST\n"
"LOAD_CONST\n"
"BINARY_ADD\n"
"RETURN_VALUE"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:736
msgid ""
"The various display tools in the :mod:`dis` module have been rewritten to "
"use these new components."
msgstr ""
"Různé nástroje zobrazování v modulu :mod:`dis` byly přepsané tak, aby "
"používaly tyto nové komponenty."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:739
msgid ""
"In addition, a new application-friendly class :class:`~dis.Bytecode` "
"provides an object-oriented API for inspecting bytecode in both in human-"
"readable form and for iterating over instructions.  The "
":class:`~dis.Bytecode` constructor takes the same arguments that "
":func:`~dis.get_instructions` does (plus an optional *current_offset*), and "
"the resulting object can be iterated to produce :class:`~dis.Instruction` "
"objects.  But it also has a :mod:`~dis.Bytecode.dis` method, equivalent to "
"calling :mod:`~dis.dis` on the constructor argument, but returned as a "
"multi-line string::"
msgstr ""
"Kromě toho nova aplikací pivřeteľová třída :class:`~dis.Bytecode` poskytuje "
"objektově orientované API pro inspektor bytecode v lidsky čitelelné formě a "
"pro iteraci přes pokyny. Konstruktor :class:`~dis.Bytecode` má stejné "
"argumenty jako :func:`~dis.get_instructions` (plus volitelné "
"*current_offset*), a výsledný objekt lze iterovat, aby se produkované "
"objekty :class:`~dis.Instruction`. Ale má také metodu "
":mod:`~dis.Bytecode.dis`, ekvivalentní volání :mod:`~dis.dis` na argumentu "
"konstruktoru, ale vráceného jako víceřádkový řetězec::"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:748
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> bytecode = dis.Bytecode(lambda x: x + 1, current_offset=3)\n"
">>> for instr in bytecode:\n"
"...     print('{} ({})'.format(instr.opname, instr.opcode))\n"
"LOAD_FAST (124)\n"
"LOAD_CONST (100)\n"
"BINARY_ADD (23)\n"
"RETURN_VALUE (83)\n"
">>> bytecode.dis().splitlines()\n"
"['  1           0 LOAD_FAST                0 (x)',\n"
" '      -->     3 LOAD_CONST               1 (1)',\n"
" '              6 BINARY_ADD',\n"
" '              7 RETURN_VALUE']"
msgstr ""
">>> bytecode = dis.Bytecode(lambda x: x + 1, current_offset=3)\n"
">>> for instr in bytecode:\n"
"...     print('{} ({})'.format(instr.opname, instr.opcode))\n"
"LOAD_FAST (124)\n"
"LOAD_CONST (100)\n"
"BINARY_ADD (23)\n"
"RETURN_VALUE (83)\n"
">>> bytecode.dis().splitlines()\n"
"['  1           0 LOAD_FAST                0 (x)',\n"
" '      -->     3 LOAD_CONST               1 (1)',\n"
" '              6 BINARY_ADD',\n"
" '              7 RETURN_VALUE']"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:761
msgid ""
":class:`~dis.Bytecode` also has a class method, "
":meth:`~dis.Bytecode.from_traceback`, that provides the ability to "
"manipulate a traceback (that is, "
"``print(Bytecode.from_traceback(tb).dis())`` is equivalent to "
"``distb(tb)``)."
msgstr ""
":class:`~dis.Bytecode` má také metodu třídy "
":meth:`~dis.Bytecode.from_traceback`, která poskytuje schopnost manipulovat "
"trasováním (to znamená, ``print(Bytecode.from_traceback(tb).dis())`` je "
"ekvivalentní ``distb(tb)``)."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:766
msgid ""
"(Contributed by Nick Coghlan, Ryan Kelly and Thomas Kluyver in "
":issue:`11816` and Claudiu Popa in :issue:`17916`.)"
msgstr ""
"(Přispěli Nick Coghlan, Ryan Kelly a Thomas Kluyver v :issue:`11816` a "
"Claudiu Popa v :issue:`17916`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:769
msgid ""
"New function :func:`~dis.stack_effect` computes the effect on the Python "
"stack of a given opcode and argument, information that is not otherwise "
"available. (Contributed by Larry Hastings in :issue:`19722`.)"
msgstr ""
"Nová funkce :func:`~dis.stack_effect` počítá efekt na zásobník Python daného"
" opcode a argumentu, informace, která jinak není dostupná. (Přispěl Larry "
"Hastings v :issue:`19722`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:775
msgid "doctest"
msgstr "doctest"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:777
msgid ""
"A new :ref:`option flag <doctest-options>`, :const:`~doctest.FAIL_FAST`, "
"halts test running as soon as the first failure is detected.  (Contributed "
"by R. David Murray and Daniel Urban in :issue:`16522`.)"
msgstr ""
"Nova :ref:`moznost s priznákem <doctest-options>`, "
":const:`~doctest.FAIL_FAST`, zastavuje beh testu hned jak se zjisti prvni "
"selhani. (Prispeli R. David Murray a Daniel Urban v :issue:`16522`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:781
msgid ""
"The :mod:`doctest` command line interface now uses :mod:`argparse`, and has "
"two new options, ``-o`` and ``-f``.  ``-o`` allows :ref:`doctest options "
"<doctest-options>` to be specified on the command line, and ``-f`` is a "
"shorthand for ``-o FAIL_FAST`` (to parallel the similar option supported by "
"the :mod:`unittest` CLI).  (Contributed by R. David Murray in "
":issue:`11390`.)"
msgstr ""
"Rozhrani prikkazoveho radu :mod:`doctest` nynı pouzıva :mod:`argparse` a ma "
"dve nove moznosti, ``-o`` a ``-f``. ``-o`` umoznuje :ref:`moznosti doctest "
"<doctest-options>` byt specifikov ny na prikazovem radu a ``-f`` je "
"zkracenina pro ``-o FAIL_FAST`` (aby paralelizoval podobnou moznost "
"podporovanou :mod:`unittest` CLI). (Prispel R. David Murray v "
":issue:`11390`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:787
msgid ""
":mod:`doctest` will now find doctests in extension module ``__doc__`` "
"strings. (Contributed by Zachary Ware in :issue:`3158`.)"
msgstr ""
":mod:`doctest` nynı najde doctesty v ``__doc__`` retezcích rozsirovacího "
"modulu. (Prispel Zachary Ware v :issue:`3158`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:792
msgid "email"
msgstr "email"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:794
msgid ""
":meth:`~email.message.Message.as_string` now accepts a *policy* argument to "
"override the default policy of the message when generating a string "
"representation of it.  This means that ``as_string`` can now be used in more"
" circumstances, instead of having to create and use a "
":mod:`~email.generator` in order to pass formatting parameters to its "
"``flatten`` method.  (Contributed by R. David Murray in :issue:`18600`.)"
msgstr ""
":meth:`~email.message.Message.as_string` nynı prijima argument *policy* k "
"prepsan í vychozi politiky spravy pri generovani jeji reprezentace retezce. "
"To znamena, ze ``as_string`` lze nynı pouzit v dalších situacích, místo aby "
"se muselo vytvaaret a pouzivat :mod:`~email.generator` aby se predaly "
"parametry formatovani jeho metode ``flatten``. (Prispel R. David Murray v "
":issue:`18600`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:801
msgid ""
"New method :meth:`~email.message.Message.as_bytes` added to produce a bytes "
"representation of the message in a fashion similar to how ``as_string`` "
"produces a string representation.  It does not accept the *maxheaderlen* "
"argument, but does accept the *unixfrom* and *policy* arguments. The "
":class:`~email.message.Message` :meth:`~email.message.Message.__bytes__` "
"method calls it, meaning that ``bytes(mymsg)`` will now produce the "
"intuitive result:  a bytes object containing the fully formatted message.  "
"(Contributed by R. David Murray in :issue:`18600`.)"
msgstr ""
"Nova metoda :meth:`~email.message.Message.as_bytes` pridana pro vytvoreni "
"bytes reprezentace spravy podobnym zpusobem, jakym ``as_string`` vyrabi "
"reprezentaci retezce. Neprijima argument *maxheaderlen*, ale prijima "
"argumenty *unixfrom* a *policy*. Metoda :class:`~email.message.Message` "
":meth:`~email.message.Message.__bytes__` ji vola, coz znamena, ze "
"``bytes(mymsg)`` nyní produkuje intuitivní výsledek: bytes objekt obsahující"
" plně formátovanou zprávu. (Prispel R. David Murray v :issue:`18600`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:810
msgid ""
"The :meth:`.Message.set_param` message now accepts a *replace* keyword "
"argument. When specified, the associated header will be updated without "
"changing its location in the list of headers.  For backward compatibility, "
"the default is ``False``.  (Contributed by R. David Murray in "
":issue:`18891`.)"
msgstr ""
"Metoda :meth:`.Message.set_param` spravy nyní prijima argument *replace* s "
"klicem. Je-li zadano, bude pridrzena zahlavi aktualizovana bez zmeny jejiho "
"umisteni v seznamu zahlavi. Pro zpetné kompatibilitu je vychozi hodnota "
"``False``. (Prispel R. David Murray v :issue:`18891`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:818
msgid ""
"A pair of new subclasses of :class:`~email.message.Message` have been added "
"(:class:`.EmailMessage` and :class:`.MIMEPart`), along with a new sub-"
"module, :mod:`~email.contentmanager` and a new :mod:`~email.policy` "
"attribute :attr:`~email.policy.EmailPolicy.content_manager`.  All "
"documentation is currently in the new module, which is being added as part "
"of email's new :term:`provisional API`.  These classes provide a number of "
"new methods that make extracting content from and inserting content into "
"email messages much easier.  For details, see the "
":mod:`~email.contentmanager` documentation and the :ref:`email-examples`.  "
"These API additions complete the bulk of the work that was planned as part "
"of the email6 project.  The currently provisional API is scheduled to become"
" final in Python 3.5 (possibly with a few minor additions in the area of "
"error handling).  (Contributed by R. David Murray in :issue:`18891`.)"
msgstr ""
"Dvojice novych podtrid :class:`~email.message.Message` byla pridana "
"(:class:`.EmailMessage` a :class:`.MIMEPart`), spolu s novym podmodulem "
":mod:`~email.contentmanager` a novy :mod:`~email.policy` atribut "
":attr:`~email.policy.EmailPolicy.content_manager`. Veskera dokumentace je v "
"soucasne chvili v novem modulu, ktery se pridava jako soucast emailu noveho "
":term:`provizorniho API`. Tyto tridy poskytují radu novych metod, ktere "
"usnadnují extrahování obsahu z a vlozéní obsahu do e-mailovych zprav. "
"Podrobnosti viz dokumentace :mod:`~email.contentmanager` a :ref:`email-"
"examples`. Tato pridani API dokoncuji prevaznou cast prace, ktera byla "
"planovna jako soucast projektu email6. V soucasne chvili provizorni API je "
"naplanovano, aby se stalo definitivnim v Pythonu 3.5 (mozna s nekolika "
"malymi prida  vkami v oblasti zpracovani chyb). (Prispel R. David Murray v "
":issue:`18891`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:834
msgid "filecmp"
msgstr "filecmp"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:836
msgid ""
"A new :func:`~filecmp.clear_cache` function provides the ability to clear "
"the :mod:`filecmp` comparison cache, which uses :func:`os.stat` information "
"to determine if the file has changed since the last compare.  This can be "
"used, for example, if the file might have been changed and re-checked in "
"less time than the resolution of a particular filesystem's file modification"
" time field. (Contributed by Mark Levitt in :issue:`18149`.)"
msgstr ""
"Nova funkce :func:`~filecmp.clear_cache` poskytuje schopnost vymazat "
"mezipamet srovnani :mod:`filecmp`, ktera pouziva informace :func:`os.stat` k"
" urceni, zda se soubor zmenil od posledniho srovnani. To lze pouzit, "
"napríkıad pokud by se soubor mohl zmenit a znovu zkontrolovat v kratsim "
"case, nez je rozliseni pole casu zmeny souboru konkretniho systemu souboru. "
"(Prispel Mark Levitt v :issue:`18149`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:843
msgid ""
"New module attribute :const:`~filecmp.DEFAULT_IGNORES` provides the list of "
"directories that are used as the default value for the *ignore* parameter of"
" the :func:`~filecmp.dircmp` function.  (Contributed by Eli Bendersky in "
":issue:`15442`.)"
msgstr ""
"Novy atribut modulu :const:`~filecmp.DEFAULT_IGNORES` poskytuje seznam "
"adresaru, ktere se pouzivaji jako vychozi hodnota parametru *ignore* funkce "
":func:`~filecmp.dircmp`. (Prispel Eli Bendersky v :issue:`15442`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:850
msgid "functools"
msgstr "functools"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:852
msgid ""
"The new :func:`~functools.partialmethod` descriptor brings partial argument "
"application to descriptors, just as :func:`~functools.partial` provides for "
"normal callables. The new descriptor also makes it easier to get arbitrary "
"callables (including :func:`~functools.partial` instances) to behave like "
"normal instance methods when included in a class definition. (Contributed by"
" Alon Horev and Nick Coghlan in :issue:`4331`.)"
msgstr ""
"Novy deskriptor :func:`~functools.partialmethod` prinasi castecnou aplikaci "
"argumentu k deskriptorum, stejne jako :func:`~functools.partial` poskytuje "
"pro normalni callable. Novy deskriptor take usnadnuje ziskani libovolnych "
"callable (vcetne instanci :func:`~functools.partial`) chovat se jako "
"normalni metody instance, kdy jsou zahrnuty v definici tridy. (Prispeli Alon"
" Horev a Nick Coghlan v :issue:`4331`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:861
msgid ""
"The new :func:`~functools.singledispatch` decorator brings support for "
"single-dispatch generic functions to the Python standard library. Where "
"object oriented programming focuses on grouping multiple operations on a "
"common set of data into a class, a generic function focuses on grouping "
"multiple implementations of an operation that allows it to work with "
"*different* kinds of data."
msgstr ""
"Novy dekorator :func:`~functools.singledispatch` prinasi podporu single-"
"dispatch generickych funkcí do standardni knihovny Pythonu. Zatimco "
"objektove orientovane programovani se zameruje na seskupeni vice operaci na "
"spolecne sade dat do tridy, genericka funkce se zameruje na seskupeni vice "
"implementaci operace, ktere ji umoznuji pracovat s *ruznymi* druhy dat."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:870
msgid ":pep:`443` -- Single-dispatch generic functions"
msgstr ":pep:`443` -- Single-dispatch genericke funkce"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:871
msgid "PEP written and implemented by Łukasz Langa."
msgstr "PEP napsan a implementovan Lukaszem Langou."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:873
msgid ""
":func:`~functools.total_ordering` now supports a return value of "
":data:`NotImplemented` from the underlying comparison function.  "
"(Contributed by Katie Miller in :issue:`10042`.)"
msgstr ""
":func:`~functools.total_ordering` nyni podporuje navratovou hodnotu "
":data:`NotImplemented` z podkladove funkce porovnani. (Prispela Katie Miller"
" v :issue:`10042`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:877
msgid ""
"A pure-python version of the :func:`~functools.partial` function is now in "
"the stdlib; in CPython it is overridden by the C accelerated version, but it"
" is available for other implementations to use.  (Contributed by Brian "
"Thorne in :issue:`12428`.)"
msgstr ""
"Cista pythonska verze funkce :func:`~functools.partial` je nyní v stdlib; v "
"CPythonu je prepsan verzí zrychlenou v C, ale je dostupna pro pouziti "
"dalších implementacích. (Prispel Brian Thorne v :issue:`12428`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:884
msgid "gc"
msgstr "gc"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:886
msgid ""
"New function :func:`~gc.get_stats` returns a list of three per-generation "
"dictionaries containing the collections statistics since interpreter "
"startup. (Contributed by Antoine Pitrou in :issue:`16351`.)"
msgstr ""
"Nova funkce :func:`~gc.get_stats` vraci seznam tri slovniku pro generaci "
"obsahujici statistiku kolekci od spusteni interpreta. (Prispel Antoine "
"Pitrou v :issue:`16351`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:892
msgid "glob"
msgstr "glob"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:894
msgid ""
"A new function :func:`~glob.escape` provides a way to escape special "
"characters in a filename so that they do not become part of the globbing "
"expansion but are instead matched literally.  (Contributed by Serhiy "
"Storchaka in :issue:`8402`.)"
msgstr ""
"Nova funkce :func:`~glob.escape` poskytuje způsob, jak se vyhnout specialnim"
" znakum v nazvu souboru, aby se nestaly soucastí rozvoje globbing, ale miste"
" toho se shodují doslova. (Prispel Serhiy Storchaka v :issue:`8402`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:900
msgid "hashlib"
msgstr "hashlib"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:902
msgid ""
"A new :func:`hashlib.pbkdf2_hmac` function provides the `PKCS#5 password-"
"based key derivation function 2 <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PBKDF2>`_.  "
"(Contributed by Christian Heimes in :issue:`18582`.)"
msgstr ""
"Nova funkce :func:`hashlib.pbkdf2_hmac` poskytuje `PKCS#5 password-based key"
" derivation function 2 <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PBKDF2>`_. (Prispel "
"Christian Heimes v :issue:`18582`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:907
msgid ""
"The :attr:`~hashlib.hash.name` attribute of :mod:`hashlib` hash objects is "
"now a formally supported interface.  It has always existed in CPython's "
":mod:`hashlib` (although it did not return lower case names for all "
"supported hashes), but it was not a public interface and so some other "
"Python implementations have not previously supported it.  (Contributed by "
"Jason R. Coombs in :issue:`18532`.)"
msgstr ""
"Atribut :attr:`~hashlib.hash.name` objektu hash :mod:`hashlib` je nyní "
"formalne podporovane rozhrani. Vzdy existovalo v CPythonu :mod:`hashlib` "
"(ackoli nevracelo mala pismena pro všechny podporovane hashe), ale nebylo to"
" verejne rozhrani, a proto nektere dalsi implementace Pythonu jej drive "
"nepodporovaly. (Prispel Jason R. Coombs v :issue:`18532`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:916
msgid "hmac"
msgstr "hmac"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:918
msgid ""
":mod:`hmac` now accepts ``bytearray`` as well as ``bytes`` for the *key* "
"argument to the :func:`~hmac.new` function, and the *msg* parameter to both "
"the :func:`~hmac.new` function and the :meth:`~hmac.HMAC.update` method now "
"accepts any type supported by the :mod:`hashlib` module.  (Contributed by "
"Jonas Borgström in :issue:`18240`.)"
msgstr ""
":mod:`hmac` nyní prijima ``bytearray`` stejne jako ``bytes`` pro argument "
"*key* funkce :func:`~hmac.new` a parametr *msg* jak funkce "
":func:`~hmac.new`, tak metody :meth:`~hmac.HMAC.update` nyní prijima "
"jakykoli typ podporovany modulem :mod:`hashlib`. (Prispel Jonas Borgstrom v "
":issue:`18240`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:924
msgid ""
"The *digestmod* argument to the :func:`hmac.new` function may now be any "
"hash digest name recognized by :mod:`hashlib`.  In addition, the current "
"behavior in which the value of *digestmod* defaults to ``MD5`` is "
"deprecated: in a future version of Python there will be no default value.  "
"(Contributed by Christian Heimes in :issue:`17276`.)"
msgstr ""
"Argument *digestmod* k funkci :func:`hmac.new` muze byt nyní jakykoli nazev "
"digest hash rozpoznany :mod:`hashlib`. Navic je aktualni chovani, ve kterem "
"se hodnota *digestmod* defaulta na ``MD5``, zastarale: v budouci verzi "
"Pythonu nebude zadna vychozi hodnota. (Prispel Christian Heimes v "
":issue:`17276`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:930
msgid ""
"With the addition of :attr:`~hmac.HMAC.block_size` and "
":attr:`~hmac.HMAC.name` attributes (and the formal documentation of the "
":attr:`~hmac.HMAC.digest_size` attribute), the :mod:`hmac` module now "
"conforms fully to the :pep:`247` API. (Contributed by Christian Heimes in "
":issue:`18775`.)"
msgstr ""
"S pridanim atributu :attr:`~hmac.HMAC.block_size` a :attr:`~hmac.HMAC.name` "
"(a formalni dokumentaci atributu :attr:`~hmac.HMAC.digest_size`), modul "
":mod:`hmac` nyní plne vyhovuje API :pep:`247`. (Prispel Christian Heimes v "
":issue:`18775`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:937
msgid "html"
msgstr "html"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:939
msgid ""
"New function :func:`~html.unescape` function converts HTML5 character "
"references to the corresponding Unicode characters.  (Contributed by Ezio "
"Melotti in :issue:`2927`.)"
msgstr ""
"Nova funkce :func:`~html.unescape` funkce konvertuje HTML5 character "
"reference na odpovídajici znaky Unicode. (Prispel Ezio Melotti v "
":issue:`2927`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:943
msgid ""
":class:`~html.parser.HTMLParser` accepts a new keyword argument "
"*convert_charrefs* that, when ``True``, automatically converts all character"
" references.  For backward-compatibility, its value defaults to ``False``, "
"but it will change to ``True`` in a future version of Python, so you are "
"invited to set it explicitly and update your code to use this new feature.  "
"(Contributed by Ezio Melotti in :issue:`13633`.)"
msgstr ""
":class:`~html.parser.HTMLParser` prijima novy keyword argument "
"*convert_charrefs*, ze, kdyz je ``True``, automaticky konvertuje všechny "
"character reference. Pro zpetnou kompatibilitu je jeji hodnota vychozi na "
"``False``, ale bude se zmenit na ``True`` v budouci verzi Pythonu, takze "
"jste zvan aktualizovat vas kod na pouziti teto nove vlastnosti. (Prispel "
"Ezio Melotti v :issue:`13633`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:950
msgid ""
"The *strict* argument of :class:`~html.parser.HTMLParser` is now deprecated."
" (Contributed by Ezio Melotti in :issue:`15114`.)"
msgstr ""
"Argument *strict* :class:`~html.parser.HTMLParser` je nyní zastarale. "
"(Prispel Ezio Melotti v :issue:`15114`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:955
msgid "http"
msgstr "http"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:957
msgid ""
":meth:`~http.server.BaseHTTPRequestHandler.send_error` now accepts an "
"optional additional *explain* parameter which can be used to provide an "
"extended error description, overriding the hardcoded default if there is "
"one. This extended error description will be formatted using the "
":attr:`~http.server.BaseHTTPRequestHandler.error_message_format` attribute "
"and sent as the body of the error response. (Contributed by Karl Cow in "
":issue:`12921`.)"
msgstr ""
":meth:`~http.server.BaseHTTPRequestHandler.send_error` nyní prijima "
"volitelny dalsí argument *explain*, ktery lze pouzit k poskytnuti rozsirene "
"popisu chyby, zastine hardcoded default je-li tam. Tato rozsirena popisu "
"chyby bude formatovana pomoci atributu "
":attr:`~http.server.BaseHTTPRequestHandler.error_message_format` a poslana "
"jako telo odezvy chyby. (Prispel Karl Cow v :issue:`12921`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:965
msgid ""
"The :mod:`http.server` :ref:`command line interface <http-server-cli>` now "
"has a ``-b/--bind`` option that causes the server to listen on a specific "
"address. (Contributed by Malte Swart in :issue:`17764`.)"
msgstr ""
"Rozhrani :mod:`http.server` :ref:`prikkazovehe radu <http-server-cli>` nyní "
"ma volbu ``-b/--bind``, ktera zaprinci server poslouchat na konkretni "
"adrese. (Prispel Malte Swart v :issue:`17764`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:971
msgid "idlelib and IDLE"
msgstr "idlelib a IDLE"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:973
msgid ""
"Since idlelib implements the IDLE shell and editor and is not intended for "
"import by other programs, it gets improvements with every release. See "
":file:`Lib/idlelib/NEWS.txt` for a cumulative list of changes since 3.3.0, "
"as well as changes made in future 3.4.x releases. This file is also "
"available from the IDLE :menuselection:`Help --> About IDLE` dialog."
msgstr ""
"Aby idlelib implementuje IDLE shell a editor a není urcen k importu jinymi "
"programy, dostava zlepseni s kazdym vydanim. Viz "
":file:`Lib/idlelib/NEWS.txt` pro kumulativni seznam zmen od 3.3.0, stejne "
"jako zmeny provedene v budoucích vydanich 3.4.x. Tento soubor je take "
"dostupny z IDLE :menuselection:`Help --> About IDLE` dialogu."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:981
msgid "importlib"
msgstr "importlib"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:983
msgid ""
"The :class:`~importlib.abc.InspectLoader` ABC defines a new method, "
":meth:`~importlib.abc.InspectLoader.source_to_code` that accepts source data"
" and a path and returns a code object.  The default implementation is "
"equivalent to ``compile(data, path, 'exec', dont_inherit=True)``. "
"(Contributed by Eric Snow and Brett Cannon in :issue:`15627`.)"
msgstr ""
":class:`~importlib.abc.InspectLoader` ABC definuje novou metodu, "
":meth:`~importlib.abc.InspectLoader.source_to_code`, ktera prijima zdrojova "
"data a cestu a vraci kod objekt. Vychozi implementace je ekvivalentní "
"``compile(data, path, 'exec', dont_inherit=True)``. (Prispeli Eric Snow a "
"Brett Cannon v :issue:`15627`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:989
msgid ""
":class:`~importlib.abc.InspectLoader` also now has a default implementation "
"for the :meth:`~importlib.abc.InspectLoader.get_code` method.  However, it "
"will normally be desirable to override the default implementation for "
"performance reasons.  (Contributed by Brett Cannon in :issue:`18072`.)"
msgstr ""
":class:`~importlib.abc.InspectLoader` nyní ma take vychozi implementaci "
"metody :meth:`~importlib.abc.InspectLoader.get_code`. Vsak to normalne bude "
"zadouce pretizit vychozi implementaci z duvodu vykonu. (Prispel Brett Cannon"
" v :issue:`18072`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:994
msgid ""
"The :func:`~importlib.reload` function has been moved from :mod:`!imp` to "
":mod:`importlib` as part of the :mod:`!imp` module deprecation.  "
"(Contributed by Berker Peksag in :issue:`18193`.)"
msgstr ""
"Funkce :func:`~importlib.reload` byla prenesena z :mod:`!imp` do "
":mod:`importlib` jako soucast deprecace modulu :mod:`!imp`. (Prispel Berker "
"Peksag v :issue:`18193`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:998
msgid ""
":mod:`importlib.util` now has a :const:`~importlib.util.MAGIC_NUMBER` "
"attribute providing access to the bytecode version number.  This replaces "
"the :func:`!get_magic` function in the deprecated :mod:`!imp` module. "
"(Contributed by Brett Cannon in :issue:`18192`.)"
msgstr ""
":mod:`importlib.util` nyní ma :const:`~importlib.util.MAGIC_NUMBER` atribut "
"poskytující pristup k cislu verze bytecode. To nahradi funkci "
":func:`!get_magic` v zastaralem modulu :mod:`!imp`. (Prispel Brett Cannon v "
":issue:`18192`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1003
msgid ""
"New :mod:`importlib.util` functions "
":func:`~importlib.util.cache_from_source` and "
":func:`~importlib.util.source_from_cache` replace the same-named functions "
"in the deprecated :mod:`!imp` module.  (Contributed by Brett Cannon in "
":issue:`18194`.)"
msgstr ""
"Nove funkce :mod:`importlib.util` :func:`~importlib.util.cache_from_source` "
"a :func:`~importlib.util.source_from_cache` nahradiji stejne pojmenovane "
"funkce v zastaralem :mod:`!imp` modulu. (Prispel Brett Cannon v "
":issue:`18194`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1008
msgid ""
"The :mod:`importlib` bootstrap :class:`.NamespaceLoader` now conforms to the"
" :class:`.InspectLoader` ABC, which means that ``runpy`` and ``python -m`` "
"can now be used with namespace packages.  (Contributed by Brett Cannon in "
":issue:`18058`.)"
msgstr ""
"Jednotka :mod:`importlib` bootstrap :class:`.NamespaceLoader` nyní odpovídá "
"ABC :class:`.InspectLoader`, coz znamena, ze ``runpy`` a ``python -m`` mohou"
" byt pouzity s namespace balicky. (Prispel Brett Cannon v :issue:`18058`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1013
msgid ""
":mod:`importlib.util` has a new function "
":func:`~importlib.util.decode_source` that decodes source from bytes using "
"universal newline processing.  This is useful for implementing "
":meth:`.InspectLoader.get_source` methods."
msgstr ""
":mod:`importlib.util` ma novou funkci :func:`~importlib.util.decode_source`,"
" ktera dekoduje zdroj z bajtu pomoci univerzalniho zpracovani novych radku. "
"To je uzitecne pro implementaci metod :meth:`.InspectLoader.get_source`."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1017
msgid ""
":class:`importlib.machinery.ExtensionFileLoader` now has a "
":meth:`~importlib.machinery.ExtensionFileLoader.get_filename` method.  This "
"was inadvertently omitted in the original implementation.  (Contributed by "
"Eric Snow in :issue:`19152`.)"
msgstr ""
":class:`importlib.machinery.ExtensionFileLoader` nyní ma metodu "
":meth:`~importlib.machinery.ExtensionFileLoader.get_filename`. To bylo "
"omylem vynechano v puvodni implementaci. (Prispel Eric Snow v "
":issue:`19152`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1024
msgid "inspect"
msgstr "inspect"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1026
msgid ""
"The :mod:`inspect` module now offers a basic :ref:`command line interface "
"<inspect-module-cli>` to quickly display source code and other information "
"for modules, classes and functions.  (Contributed by Claudiu Popa and Nick "
"Coghlan in :issue:`18626`.)"
msgstr ""
"Modul :mod:`inspect` nyní nabizí zakladni :ref:`rozhrani prikkazoveho radu "
"<inspect-module-cli>` k rychlemému zobrazení zdrojoveho kodu a dalsich "
"informaci pro moduly, tridy a funkce. (Prispeli Claudiu Popa a Nick Coghlan "
"v :issue:`18626`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1031
msgid ""
":func:`~inspect.unwrap` makes it easy to unravel wrapper function chains "
"created by :func:`functools.wraps` (and any other API that sets the "
"``__wrapped__`` attribute on a wrapper function).  (Contributed by Daniel "
"Urban, Aaron Iles and Nick Coghlan in :issue:`13266`.)"
msgstr ""
":func:`~inspect.unwrap` usnadnuje odmotani retezcu funkcio obalitelne "
"vytvorene :func:`functools.wraps` (a jakymkoli jinym API, ktere nastavuje "
"atribut ``__wrapped__`` na funkci obalu). (Prispeli Daniel Urban, Aaron Iles"
" a Nick Coghlan v :issue:`13266`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1036
msgid ""
"As part of the implementation of the new :mod:`enum` module, the "
":mod:`inspect` module now has substantially better support for custom "
"``__dir__`` methods and dynamic class attributes provided through "
"metaclasses.  (Contributed by Ethan Furman in :issue:`18929` and "
":issue:`19030`.)"
msgstr ""
"Jako soucast implementace noveho modulu :mod:`enum`, modul :mod:`inspect` "
"nyní ma podstatne lepsi podporu pro vlastni ``__dir__`` metody a dynamicke "
"atributy tridy poskytovane prostrednictvim metaklas. (Prispel Ethan Furman v"
" :issue:`18929` a :issue:`19030`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1042
msgid ""
":func:`~inspect.getfullargspec` and :func:`!getargspec` now use the "
":func:`~inspect.signature` API. This allows them to support a much broader "
"range of callables, including those with ``__signature__`` attributes, those"
" with metadata provided by argument clinic, :func:`functools.partial` "
"objects and more. Note that, unlike :func:`~inspect.signature`, these "
"functions still ignore ``__wrapped__`` attributes, and report the already "
"bound first argument for bound methods, so it is still necessary to update "
"your code to use :func:`~inspect.signature` directly if those features are "
"desired. (Contributed by Yury Selivanov in :issue:`17481`.)"
msgstr ""
":func:`~inspect.getfullargspec` a :func:`!getargspec` nyní pouzivaji API "
":func:`~inspect.signature`. To jim umoznuje podporovat mnohem sirsi rozsah "
"callable, vcetne tech s atributy ``__signature__``, tech s metadaty "
"poskytovanymi argument clinic, objekty :func:`functools.partial` a vice. "
"Poznamka, ze na rozdil od :func:`~inspect.signature`, tyto funkce stale "
"ignoruji atributy ``__wrapped__`` a hlasi uz vyznam prvni argument pro "
"metody vyznam, takze je stale nutne aktualizovat vas kod na pouziti "
":func:`~inspect.signature` primo, pokud jsou tyto vlastnosti zadouci. "
"(Prispel Yury Selivanov v :issue:`17481`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1053
msgid ""
":func:`~inspect.signature` now supports duck types of CPython functions, "
"which adds support for functions compiled with Cython.  (Contributed by "
"Stefan Behnel and Yury Selivanov in :issue:`17159`.)"
msgstr ""
":func:`~inspect.signature` nyní podporuje kachni typy funkcí CPython, coz "
"zvysuje podporu pro funkce kompilovane s Cython. (Prispeli Stefan Behnel a "
"Yury Selivanov v :issue:`17159`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1059
msgid "ipaddress"
msgstr "ipaddress"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1061
msgid ""
":mod:`ipaddress` was added to the standard library in Python 3.3 as a "
":term:`provisional API`. With the release of Python 3.4, this qualification "
"has been removed: :mod:`ipaddress` is now considered a stable API, covered "
"by the normal standard library requirements to maintain backwards "
"compatibility."
msgstr ""
":mod:`ipaddress` byl pridan do standardni knihovny v Pythonu 3.3 jako "
":term:`provizorni API`. S vydanim Pythonu 3.4 byla tato kvalifikace "
"odstranena: :mod:`ipaddress` je nyní povazovan za stabilni API, pokryty "
"normalnima pozadavky standardni knihovny na udrzeni zpatne kompatibility."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1067
msgid ""
"A new :attr:`~ipaddress.IPv4Address.is_global` property is ``True`` if an "
"address is globally routeable.  (Contributed by Peter Moody in "
":issue:`17400`.)"
msgstr ""
"Nova vlastnost :attr:`~ipaddress.IPv4Address.is_global` je ``True`` pokud je"
" adresa globalne smerovatelen. (Prispel Peter Moody v :issue:`17400`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1073
msgid "logging"
msgstr "logging"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1075
msgid ""
"The :class:`~logging.handlers.TimedRotatingFileHandler` has a new *atTime* "
"parameter that can be used to specify the time of day when rollover should "
"happen.  (Contributed by Ronald Oussoren in :issue:`9556`.)"
msgstr ""
":class:`~logging.handlers.TimedRotatingFileHandler` ma novy parametr "
"*atTime*, ktery lze pouzit k urceni casu dne, kdy by mel dojit rollover. "
"(Prispel Ronald Oussoren v :issue:`9556`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1079
msgid ""
":class:`~logging.handlers.SocketHandler` and "
":class:`~logging.handlers.DatagramHandler` now support Unix domain sockets "
"(by setting *port* to ``None``).  (Contributed by Vinay Sajip in commit "
"ce46195b56a9.)"
msgstr ""
":class:`~logging.handlers.SocketHandler` a "
":class:`~logging.handlers.DatagramHandler` nyní podporuji Unix domain "
"sockety (nastavením *port* na ``None``). (Prispel Vinay Sajip v commit "
"ce46195b56a9.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1084
msgid ""
":func:`~logging.config.fileConfig` now accepts a "
":class:`configparser.RawConfigParser` subclass instance for the *fname* "
"parameter.  This facilitates using a configuration file when logging "
"configuration is just a part of the overall application configuration, or "
"where the application modifies the configuration before passing it to "
":func:`~logging.config.fileConfig`.  (Contributed by Vinay Sajip in "
":issue:`16110`.)"
msgstr ""
":func:`~logging.config.fileConfig` nyní prijima instanci podtridy "
":class:`configparser.RawConfigParser` pro parametr *fname*. To usnadnuje "
"pouziti konfiguracniho souboru, kdy je logovani konfigurace pouze casti cele"
" aplikace konfigurace, nebo kde aplikace modifikuje konfiguraci pred "
"predanim do :func:`~logging.config.fileConfig`. (Prispel Vinay Sajip v "
":issue:`16110`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1092
msgid ""
"Logging configuration data received from a socket via the "
":func:`logging.config.listen` function can now be validated before being "
"processed by supplying a verification function as the argument to the new "
"*verify* keyword argument.  (Contributed by Vinay Sajip in :issue:`15452`.)"
msgstr ""
"Data konfigurace logovani prijata ze socketu prostrednictvim funkce "
":func:`logging.config.listen` mohou byt nyní overena pred zpracovanim "
"zadanim funkce overeni jako argument nove klicove slovo *verify*. (Prispel "
"Vinay Sajip v :issue:`15452`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1101
msgid "marshal"
msgstr "marshal"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1103
msgid ""
"The default :mod:`marshal` version has been bumped to 3.  The code "
"implementing the new version restores the Python2 behavior of recording only"
" one copy of interned strings and preserving the interning on "
"deserialization, and extends this \"one copy\" ability to any object type "
"(including handling recursive references).  This reduces both the size of "
"``.pyc`` files and the amount of memory a module occupies in memory when it "
"is loaded from a ``.pyc`` (or ``.pyo``) file.  (Contributed by Kristján "
"Valur Jónsson in :issue:`16475`, with additional speedups by Antoine Pitrou "
"in :issue:`19219`.)"
msgstr ""
"Vychozi verze :mod:`marshal` byla zvysena na 3. Kod implementujici novou "
"verzi obnovi chovaní Python2 zaznamenavanivani pouze jedne kopie "
"internazovanych retezcu a zachovani internazovani pri deserialisaci, a "
"rozsiruje tuto \"jednu kopii\" schopnost na jakykoli typ objektu (vcetne "
"zpracovani rekurzivnich odkazu). To snizuje jak velikost souboru ``.pyc``, "
"tak pokud je mnozstvi pameti modul zabirá v pameti, kdyz je nacten ze "
"souboru ``.pyc`` (nebo ``.pyo``). (Prispel Kristjan Valur Jonsson v "
":issue:`16475`, s dodatecnym zrychlenm od Antoine Pitrou v :issue:`19219`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1114
msgid "mmap"
msgstr "mmap"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1116
msgid ""
"mmap objects are now :ref:`weakly referenceable <mod-weakref>`. (Contributed"
" by Valerie Lambert in :issue:`4885`.)"
msgstr ""
"Objekty mmap jsou nyní :ref:`slabe referencovane <mod-weakref>`. (Prispela "
"Valerie Lambert v :issue:`4885`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1121
msgid "multiprocessing"
msgstr "multiprocessing"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1125
msgid ""
"On Unix two new :ref:`start methods <multiprocessing-start-methods>`, "
"``spawn`` and ``forkserver``, have been added for starting processes using "
":mod:`multiprocessing`.  These make the mixing of processes with threads "
"more robust, and the ``spawn`` method matches the semantics that "
"multiprocessing has always used on Windows.  New function "
":func:`~multiprocessing.get_all_start_methods` reports all start methods "
"available on the platform, :func:`~multiprocessing.get_start_method` reports"
" the current start method, and :func:`~multiprocessing.set_start_method` "
"sets the start method.  (Contributed by Richard Oudkerk in :issue:`8713`.)"
msgstr ""
"Na Unix dva nove :ref:`pocatecni metody <multiprocessing-start-methods>`, "
"``spawn`` a ``forkserver``, byly pridan pro spusteni procesu pouzitim "
":mod:`multiprocessing`. Ty cini smisovani procesu s vlakny robustnejsim, a "
"metoda ``spawn`` se shoduje se semantikou, kterou multiprocessing vzdy "
"pouzival na Windows. Nova funkce "
":func:`~multiprocessing.get_all_start_methods` hlasi vsechny dostupne "
"pocatecni metody na platforme, :func:`~multiprocessing.get_start_method` "
"hlasi aktualni pocatecni metodu, a :func:`~multiprocessing.set_start_method`"
" nastavuje pocatecni metodu. (Prispel Richard Oudkerk v :issue:`8713`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1135
msgid ""
":mod:`multiprocessing` also now has the concept of a ``context``, which "
"determines how child processes are created.  New function "
":func:`~multiprocessing.get_context` returns a context that uses a specified"
" start method.  It has the same API as the :mod:`multiprocessing` module "
"itself, so you can use it to create :class:`~multiprocessing.pool.Pool`\\ s "
"and other objects that will operate within that context.  This allows a "
"framework and an application or different parts of the same application to "
"use multiprocessing without interfering with each other.  (Contributed by "
"Richard Oudkerk in :issue:`18999`.)"
msgstr ""
":mod:`multiprocessing` take nyní ma koncept ``kontext``, ktery urcuje, jak "
"jsou vytvoreny podprocesy. Nova funkce :func:`~multiprocessing.get_context` "
"vraci kontext, ktery pouziva zadanou pocatecni metodu. Ma stejne API jako "
"samotny modul :mod:`multiprocessing`, takze ho muze pouzit k vytvoreni "
":class:`~multiprocessing.pool.Pool`\\ s a ostatnich objektu, ktere budou "
"pracovat v tom kontextu. To umoznuje rozhrani a aplikaci nebo rozdilne casti"
" stejne aplikace pouzivat multiprocessing bez interferenci s sebou navzajem."
" (Prispel Richard Oudkerk v :issue:`18999`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1145
msgid ""
"Except when using the old *fork* start method, child processes no longer "
"inherit unneeded handles/file descriptors from their parents (part of "
":issue:`8713`)."
msgstr ""
"S vyjimkou pouziti stare pocatecni metody *fork*, podprocesy jiz nede di "
"nepotrebne manipulatoy/deskriptory souboru od jejich rodicu (soucast "
":issue:`8713`)."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1149
msgid ""
":mod:`multiprocessing` now relies on :mod:`runpy` (which implements the "
"``-m`` switch) to initialise ``__main__`` appropriately in child processes "
"when using the ``spawn`` or ``forkserver`` start methods. This resolves some"
" edge cases where combining multiprocessing, the ``-m`` command line switch,"
" and explicit relative imports could cause obscure failures in child "
"processes.  (Contributed by Nick Coghlan in :issue:`19946`.)"
msgstr ""
":mod:`multiprocessing` se nyní spolehá na :mod:`runpy` (ktere implementuje "
"`--m`` prepinac) na inicializaci ``__main__`` vhodne v podprocesech pri "
"pouziti ``spawn`` nebo ``forkserver`` pocatecnich metod. To resit nektere "
"hranicni pripady, kde kombinovani multiprocessing, ``-m`` prikkazoveho radu "
"prepinace, a explicitni relativni import mohou zpusobit nejasne selhani v "
"podprocesech. (Prispel Nick Coghlan v :issue:`19946`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1158
msgid "operator"
msgstr "operator"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1160
msgid ""
"New function :func:`~operator.length_hint` provides an implementation of the"
" specification for how the :meth:`~object.__length_hint__` special method "
"should be used, as part of the :pep:`424` formal specification of this "
"language feature.  (Contributed by Armin Ronacher in :issue:`16148`.)"
msgstr ""
"Nova funkce :func:`~operator.length_hint` poskytuje implementaci specifikace"
" jak by mela byt metoda :meth:`~object.__length_hint__` specialni pouzivana,"
" jako soucast formalni specifikace :pep:`424` teto vlastnosti jazyka. "
"(Prispel Armin Ronacher v :issue:`16148`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1165
msgid ""
"There is now a pure-python version of the :mod:`operator` module available "
"for reference and for use by alternate implementations of Python.  "
"(Contributed by Zachary Ware in :issue:`16694`.)"
msgstr ""
"Nyní je dostupna cista pythonska verze modulu :mod:`operator` pro referencu "
"a pouziti alternativnimi implementacemi Pythonu. (Prispel Zachary Ware v "
":issue:`16694`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1171
msgid "os"
msgstr "os"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1173
msgid ""
"There are new functions to get and set the :ref:`inheritable flag "
"<fd_inheritance>` of a file descriptor (:func:`os.get_inheritable`, "
":func:`os.set_inheritable`) or a Windows handle "
"(:func:`os.get_handle_inheritable`, :func:`os.set_handle_inheritable`)."
msgstr ""
"Existuji nove funkce k ziskani a nastaveni :ref:`dedicneho flagu "
"<fd_inheritance>` deskriptoru souboru (:func:`os.get_inheritable`, "
":func:`os.set_inheritable`) nebo Windows manipulatoru "
"(:func:`os.get_handle_inheritable`, :func:`os.set_handle_inheritable`)."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1178
msgid ""
"New function :func:`~os.cpu_count` reports the number of CPUs available on "
"the platform on which Python is running (or ``None`` if the count can't be "
"determined).  The :func:`multiprocessing.cpu_count` function is now "
"implemented in terms of this function).  (Contributed by Trent Nelson, "
"Yogesh Chaudhari, Victor Stinner, and Charles-François Natali in "
":issue:`17914`.)"
msgstr ""
"Nova funkce :func:`~os.cpu_count` hlasi pocet CPUs dostupnych na platforme, "
"na ktere Python bezi (nebo ``None`` pokud pocet nelze urcit). Funkce "
":func:`multiprocessing.cpu_count` je nyní implementovana v terminu teto "
"funkce). (Prispeli Trent Nelson, Yogesh Chaudhari, Victor Stinner a Charles-"
"Francois Natali v :issue:`17914`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1184
msgid ""
":func:`os.path.samestat` is now available on the Windows platform (and the "
":func:`os.path.samefile` implementation is now shared between Unix and "
"Windows).  (Contributed by Brian Curtin in :issue:`11939`.)"
msgstr ""
":func:`os.path.samestat` je nyní dostupna na platforme Windows (a "
"implementace :func:`os.path.samefile` je nyní sdilena mezi Unix a Windows). "
"(Prispel Brian Curtin v :issue:`11939`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1188
msgid ""
":func:`os.path.ismount` now recognizes volumes mounted below a drive root on"
" Windows.  (Contributed by Tim Golden in :issue:`9035`.)"
msgstr ""
":func:`os.path.ismount` nyní prizna svazky pripojene pod jednotkou root na "
"Windows. (Prispel Tim Golden v :issue:`9035`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1191
msgid ""
":func:`os.open` supports two new flags on platforms that provide them, "
":const:`~os.O_PATH` (un-opened file descriptor), and :const:`~os.O_TMPFILE` "
"(unnamed temporary file; as of 3.4.0 release available only on Linux systems"
" with a kernel version of 3.11 or newer that have uapi headers).  "
"(Contributed by Christian Heimes in :issue:`18673` and Benjamin Peterson, "
"respectively.)"
msgstr ""
":func:`os.open` podporuje dva nove priznaky na platformach, ktere je "
"poskytují, :const:`~os.O_PATH` (neotvorený deskriptor souboru), a "
":const:`~os.O_TMPFILE` (nepojmenovany docasny soubor; od vydani 3.4.0 "
"dostupny pouze na Linux systémech s verzí kernelu 3.11 nebo novejsi, ktere "
"mají uapi headery). (Prispeli Christian Heimes v :issue:`18673` a Benjamin "
"Peterson, v tom poradi.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1199
msgid "pdb"
msgstr "pdb"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1201
msgid ""
":mod:`pdb` has been enhanced to handle generators, :keyword:`yield`, and "
"``yield from`` in a more useful fashion.  This is especially helpful when "
"debugging :mod:`asyncio` based programs.  (Contributed by Andrew Svetlov and"
" Xavier de Gaye in :issue:`16596`.)"
msgstr ""
":mod:`pdb` byl vylepšen aby spravl generatory, :keyword:`yield` a ``yield "
"from`` uziticnym způsobem. To je obzvláště uzitecne pri ladeni programu "
"zalozeneho na :mod:`asyncio`. (Prispeli Andrew Svetlov a Xavier de Gaye v "
":issue:`16596`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1206
msgid ""
"The ``print`` command has been removed from :mod:`pdb`, restoring access to "
"the Python :func:`print` function from the pdb command line.  Python2's "
"``pdb`` did not have a ``print`` command; instead, entering ``print`` "
"executed the ``print`` statement.  In Python3 ``print`` was mistakenly made "
"an alias for the pdb :pdbcmd:`p` command.  ``p``, however, prints the "
"``repr`` of its argument, not the ``str`` like the Python2 ``print`` command"
" did.  Worse, the Python3 ``pdb print`` command shadowed the Python3 "
"``print`` function, making it inaccessible at the ``pdb`` prompt.  "
"(Contributed by Connor Osborn in :issue:`18764`.)"
msgstr ""
"Prikaz ``print`` byl odstraněn z :mod:`pdb`, obnovená pristup k Python "
"funkci :func:`print` z pdb prikkazoveho radu. Python2 ``pdb`` nemela prikaz "
"``print``; miste toho, zadavani ``print`` spustilo statment ``print``. V "
"Python3 ``print`` byla omylem ucin ena aliasem pro pdb prikaz :pdbcmd:`p`. "
"``p``, vsak, tiskne ``repr`` sveho argumentu, ne ``str`` jako Python2 "
"``print`` prikaz delal. Hure, Python3 ``pdb print`` prikaz zaclonoval "
"Python3 ``print`` funkci, cini ji nedostupnou na ``pdb`` promptu. (Prispel "
"Connor Osborn v :issue:`18764`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1220
msgid "pickle"
msgstr "pickle"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1222
msgid ""
":mod:`pickle` now supports (but does not use by default) a new pickle "
"protocol, protocol 4.  This new protocol addresses a number of issues that "
"were present in previous protocols, such as the serialization of nested "
"classes, very large strings and containers, and classes whose "
":meth:`~object.__new__` method takes keyword-only arguments.  It also "
"provides some efficiency improvements."
msgstr ""
":mod:`pickle` nyní podporuje (ale pouziva jako vychozi) novi protokol "
"pickle, protokol 4. Tento novy protokol resi pocet problemu, ktere byly "
"pritomny v predchozich protokolech, jako je serializace vnorenych trid, "
"velmi velkych retezcu a kontejneru, a trid, jejichz metoda "
":meth:`~object.__new__` bere argumenty pouze s klicem. Poskytuje take "
"nektere vylepseni cinnosti."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1230
msgid ":pep:`3154` -- Pickle protocol 4"
msgstr ":pep:`3154` -- Pickle protokol 4"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1231
msgid "PEP written by Antoine Pitrou and implemented by Alexandre Vassalotti."
msgstr "PEP napsan Antoine Pitrou a implementovan Alexandre Vassalotti."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1235
msgid "plistlib"
msgstr "plistlib"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1237
msgid ""
":mod:`plistlib` now has an API that is similar to the standard pattern for "
"stdlib serialization protocols, with new :func:`~plistlib.load`, "
":func:`~plistlib.dump`, :func:`~plistlib.loads`, and :func:`~plistlib.dumps`"
" functions.  (The older API is now deprecated.)  In addition to the already "
"supported XML plist format (:const:`~plistlib.FMT_XML`), it also now "
"supports the binary plist format (:const:`~plistlib.FMT_BINARY`).  "
"(Contributed by Ronald Oussoren and others in :issue:`14455`.)"
msgstr ""
":mod:`plistlib` nyní ma API, ktere je podobne standardnimu vzoru pro stdlib "
"serializacni protokoly, s novymi funkcemi :func:`~plistlib.load`, "
":func:`~plistlib.dump`, :func:`~plistlib.loads` a :func:`~plistlib.dumps`. "
"(Starsi API je nyní zastarale.) Krom uz podporovaneho XML plist formatu "
"(:const:`~plistlib.FMT_XML`), podporuje nyní i binarni plist format "
"(:const:`~plistlib.FMT_BINARY`). (Prispeli Ronald Oussoren a ostatni v "
":issue:`14455`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1247
msgid "poplib"
msgstr "poplib"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1249
msgid ""
"Two new methods have been added to :mod:`poplib`: :meth:`~poplib.POP3.capa`,"
" which returns the list of capabilities advertised by the POP server, and "
":meth:`~poplib.POP3.stls`, which switches a clear-text POP3 session into an "
"encrypted POP3 session if the POP server supports it.  (Contributed by "
"Lorenzo Catucci in :issue:`4473`.)"
msgstr ""
"Dve nove metody byly pridan do :mod:`poplib`: :meth:`~poplib.POP3.capa`, "
"ktera vraci seznam moznosti hlasovanych POP serverem, a "
":meth:`~poplib.POP3.stls`, ktera prepina jasny textovy POP3 relaci na "
"sifrovany POP3 relaci pokud POP server podporuje. (Prispel Lorenzo Catucci v"
" :issue:`4473`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1257
msgid "pprint"
msgstr "pprint"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1259
msgid ""
"The :mod:`pprint` module's :class:`~pprint.PrettyPrinter` class and its "
":func:`~pprint.pformat`, and :func:`~pprint.pprint` functions have a new "
"option, *compact*, that controls how the output is formatted.  Currently "
"setting *compact* to ``True`` means that sequences will be printed with as "
"many sequence elements as will fit within *width* on each (indented) line. "
"(Contributed by Serhiy Storchaka in :issue:`19132`.)"
msgstr ""
"Trida :class:`~pprint.PrettyPrinter` modulu :mod:`pprint` a jeho funkce "
":func:`~pprint.pformat` a :func:`~pprint.pprint` mají novou moznost, "
"*compact*, ktera kontroluje jak je vystup formatovan. V soucasne dobe "
"nastaveni *compact* na ``True`` znamena, ze sekvence budou tisky se tolika "
"prvky sekvence, kolik se vejde do *width* na kazdem (odsazenem) radku. "
"(Prispel Serhiy Storchaka v :issue:`19132`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1266
msgid ""
"Long strings are now wrapped using Python's normal line continuation syntax."
"  (Contributed by Antoine Pitrou in :issue:`17150`.)"
msgstr ""
"Dlouhe retezce jsou nyní zalomeny pomoci normalni syntaxe pokracovani radku "
"Pythonu. (Prispel Antoine Pitrou v :issue:`17150`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1271
msgid "pty"
msgstr "pty"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1273
msgid ""
":func:`pty.spawn` now returns the status value from :func:`os.waitpid` on "
"the child process, instead of ``None``.  (Contributed by Gregory P. Smith.)"
msgstr ""
":func:`pty.spawn` nyní vraci stavovou hodnotu z :func:`os.waitpid` na "
"podprocesu, místo ``None``. (Prispel Gregory P. Smith.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1278
msgid "pydoc"
msgstr "pydoc"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1280
msgid ""
"The :mod:`pydoc` module is now based directly on the "
":func:`inspect.signature` introspection API, allowing it to provide "
"signature information for a wider variety of callable objects. This change "
"also means that ``__wrapped__`` attributes are now taken into account when "
"displaying help information. (Contributed by Larry Hastings in "
":issue:`19674`.)"
msgstr ""
"Modul :mod:`pydoc` je nyní zalozen primo na API introspekce "
":func:`inspect.signature`, umoznujici mu poskytnout informace o signature "
"pro sirsí variaci objektu volajicich. Tato zmena take znamena, ze atributy "
"``__wrapped__`` jsou nyní brany do uvahypri zobrazovani pomoci informaci. "
"(Prispel Larry Hastings v :issue:`19674`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1286
msgid ""
"The :mod:`pydoc` module no longer displays the ``self`` parameter for "
"already bound methods. Instead, it aims to always display the exact current "
"signature of the supplied callable.  (Contributed by Larry Hastings in "
":issue:`20710`.)"
msgstr ""
"Modul :mod:`pydoc` jiz nezobrazuje parametr ``self`` pro jiz vyznam metody. "
"Namiste toho, si klade cil vzdy zobrazit presny aktualni podpis poskytnuteho"
" callable. (Prispel Larry Hastings v :issue:`20710`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1291
msgid ""
"In addition to the changes that have been made to :mod:`pydoc` directly, its"
" handling of custom ``__dir__`` methods and various descriptor behaviours "
"has also been improved substantially by the underlying changes in the "
":mod:`inspect` module."
msgstr ""
"Krome zmen, ktere byly provedy v :mod:`pydoc` primo, jeho zacloneni vlastni "
"``__dir__`` metody a ruzne chování deskriptoru bylo take vyrazne zlepseno "
"zmeny v modulu :mod:`inspect`."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1296
msgid ""
"As the :func:`help` builtin is based on :mod:`pydoc`, the above changes also"
" affect the behaviour of :func:`help`."
msgstr ""
"Jak je vestavena :func:`help` zalozena na :mod:`pydoc`, vyse uvedene zmeny "
"take ovlivnuji chování :func:`help`."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1301
msgid "re"
msgstr "re"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1303
msgid ""
"New :func:`~re.fullmatch` function and :meth:`.Pattern.fullmatch` method "
"anchor the pattern at both ends of the string to match.  This provides a way"
" to be explicit about the goal of the match, which avoids a class of subtle "
"bugs where ``$`` characters get lost during code changes or the addition of "
"alternatives to an existing regular expression.  (Contributed by Matthew "
"Barnett in :issue:`16203`.)"
msgstr ""
"Nova funkce :func:`~re.fullmatch` a metoda :meth:`.Pattern.fullmatch` "
"kotvují vzor na obou koncich retezce, aby se shodul. To poskytuje způsob, "
"jak byt explicíní cil zpáru, coz se vyhýba tride subtilnich chyb, kde se "
"znaky ``$`` ztrácejic beh zmeny kodu nebo dodatkem alternativ k existujicemu"
" regularnimu vyrazu. (Prispel Matthew Barnett v :issue:`16203`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1310
msgid ""
"The repr of :ref:`regex objects <re-objects>` now includes the pattern and "
"the flags; the repr of :ref:`match objects <match-objects>` now includes the"
" start, end, and the part of the string that matched.  (Contributed by Hugo "
"Lopes Tavares and Serhiy Storchaka in :issue:`13592` and :issue:`17087`.)"
msgstr ""
"Repr :ref:`objektu regex <re-objects>` nyní zahrnuje vzor a priznaky; repr "
":ref:`objektu zpáru <match-objects>` nyní zahrnuje zacatek, konec a cast "
"retezce, ktera se shodoval. (Prispeli Hugo Lopes Tavares a Serhiy Storchaka "
"v :issue:`13592` a :issue:`17087`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1318
msgid "resource"
msgstr "resource"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1320
msgid ""
"New :func:`~resource.prlimit` function, available on Linux platforms with a "
"kernel version of 2.6.36 or later and glibc of 2.13 or later, provides the "
"ability to query or set the resource limits for processes other than the one"
" making the call.  (Contributed by Christian Heimes in :issue:`16595`.)"
msgstr ""
"Nova funkce :func:`~resource.prlimit`, dostupna na platformach Linux s verzí"
" kernelu 2.6.36 nebo novejsi a glibc 2.13 nebo novejsi, poskytuje schopnost "
"dotazovat nebo nastavit limity zdroju pro procesy jine nez ten, ktery vola. "
"(Prispel Christian Heimes v :issue:`16595`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1325
msgid ""
"On Linux kernel version 2.6.36 or later, there are also some new Linux "
"specific constants: :const:`~resource.RLIMIT_MSGQUEUE`, "
":const:`~resource.RLIMIT_NICE`, :const:`~resource.RLIMIT_RTPRIO`, "
":const:`~resource.RLIMIT_RTTIME`, and :const:`~resource.RLIMIT_SIGPENDING`. "
"(Contributed by Christian Heimes in :issue:`19324`.)"
msgstr ""
"Na Linux kernelu verze 2.6.36 nebo novejsi, existují take nektere nove Linux"
" specifikum konstanty: :const:`~resource.RLIMIT_MSGQUEUE`, "
":const:`~resource.RLIMIT_NICE`, :const:`~resource.RLIMIT_RTPRIO`, "
":const:`~resource.RLIMIT_RTTIME` a :const:`~resource.RLIMIT_SIGPENDING`. "
"(Prispel Christian Heimes v :issue:`19324`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1331
msgid ""
"On FreeBSD version 9 and later, there some new FreeBSD specific constants: "
":const:`~resource.RLIMIT_SBSIZE`, :const:`~resource.RLIMIT_SWAP`, and "
":const:`~resource.RLIMIT_NPTS`.  (Contributed by Claudiu Popa in "
":issue:`19343`.)"
msgstr ""
"Na FreeBSD verze 9 a novejsi, jsou nektere nove FreeBSD specifiku konstanty:"
" :const:`~resource.RLIMIT_SBSIZE`, :const:`~resource.RLIMIT_SWAP` a "
":const:`~resource.RLIMIT_NPTS`. (Prispel Claudiu Popa v :issue:`19343`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1338
msgid "select"
msgstr "select"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1340
msgid ""
":class:`~select.epoll` objects now support the context management protocol. "
"When used in a :keyword:`with` statement, the :meth:`~select.epoll.close` "
"method will be called automatically at the end of the block.  (Contributed "
"by Serhiy Storchaka in :issue:`16488`.)"
msgstr ""
"Objekty :class:`~select.epoll` nyní podporuji protokol správy kontextu. Je-"
"li použito v příkazu :keyword:`with`, bude metoda "
":meth:`~select.epoll.close` volána automaticky na konci bloku. (Prispel "
"Serhiy Storchaka v :issue:`16488`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1345
msgid ""
":class:`~select.devpoll` objects now have :meth:`~select.devpoll.fileno` and"
" :meth:`~select.devpoll.close` methods, as well as a new attribute "
":attr:`~select.devpoll.closed`.  (Contributed by Victor Stinner in "
":issue:`18794`.)"
msgstr ""
"Objekty :class:`~select.devpoll` nyní mají metody "
":meth:`~select.devpoll.fileno` a :meth:`~select.devpoll.close`, stejne jako "
"novy atribut :attr:`~select.devpoll.closed`. (Prispel Victor Stinner v "
":issue:`18794`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1352
msgid "shelve"
msgstr "shelve"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1354
msgid ""
":class:`~shelve.Shelf` instances may now be used in :keyword:`with` "
"statements, and will be automatically closed at the end of the "
":keyword:`!with` block. (Contributed by Filip Gruszczyński in "
":issue:`13896`.)"
msgstr ""
"Instance :class:`~shelve.Shelf` mohou byt nyní pouzity v příkazech "
":keyword:`with` a budou automaticky uzavreny na konci :keyword:`!with` "
"bloku. (Prispel Filip Gruszczyski v :issue:`13896`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1360
msgid "shutil"
msgstr "shutil"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1362
msgid ""
":func:`~shutil.copyfile` now raises a specific :exc:`~shutil.Error` "
"subclass, :exc:`~shutil.SameFileError`, when the source and destination are "
"the same file, which allows an application to take appropriate action on "
"this specific error.  (Contributed by Atsuo Ishimoto and Hynek Schlawack in "
":issue:`1492704`.)"
msgstr ""
":func:`~shutil.copyfile` nyní vyvolava konkretni :exc:`~shutil.Error` "
"podtridu, :exc:`~shutil.SameFileError`, kdyz je zdroj a destina stejny "
"soubor, coz umoznuje aplikaci podniknout vhodne opatreni pri teto konkretni "
"chybe. (Prispeli Atsuo Ishimoto a Hynek Schlawack v :issue:`1492704`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1370
msgid "smtpd"
msgstr "smtpd"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1372
msgid ""
"The :class:`!SMTPServer` and :class:`!SMTPChannel` classes now accept a "
"*map* keyword argument which, if specified, is passed in to "
":class:`!asynchat.async_chat` as its *map* argument.  This allows an "
"application to avoid affecting the global socket map.  (Contributed by Vinay"
" Sajip in :issue:`11959`.)"
msgstr ""
"Třídy :class:`!SMTPServer` a :class:`!SMTPChannel` nyní přijíjmají argument "
"*map* s klíčem, který, je-li zadán, je předán do "
":class:`!asynchat.async_chat` jako jeho argument *map*. To umožňuje aplikaci"
" vyhnout se ovlivnění globální mapy socketů. (Přispěl Vinay Sajip v "
":issue:`11959`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1380
msgid "smtplib"
msgstr "smtplib"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1382
msgid ""
":exc:`~smtplib.SMTPException` is now a subclass of :exc:`OSError`, which "
"allows both socket level errors and SMTP protocol level errors to be caught "
"in one try/except statement by code that only cares whether or not an error "
"occurred. (Contributed by Ned Jackson Lovely in :issue:`2118`.)"
msgstr ""
":exc:`~smtplib.SMTPException` je nyní podtrida :exc:`OSError`, coz umoznuje "
"jak socket urovnove chyby, tak SMTP protokol urovnove chyby byt chyceny v "
"jednom pokusu/vyjimka prohlaseni kodem, ktery se stara pouze o to, zda doslo"
" k chybe nebo ne. (Prispel Ned Jackson Lovely v :issue:`2118`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1389
msgid "socket"
msgstr "socket"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1391
msgid ""
"The socket module now supports the :const:`~socket.CAN_BCM` protocol on "
"platforms that support it.  (Contributed by Brian Thorne in :issue:`15359`.)"
msgstr ""
"Modul socket nyní podporuje protokol :const:`~socket.CAN_BCM` na "
"platformach, ktere ji podporuji. (Prispel Brian Thorne v :issue:`15359`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1394
msgid ""
"Socket objects have new methods to get or set their :ref:`inheritable flag "
"<fd_inheritance>`, :meth:`~socket.socket.get_inheritable` and "
":meth:`~socket.socket.set_inheritable`."
msgstr ""
"Objekty Socket mají nove metody k získání nebo nastaveni jejich "
":ref:`dedicneho flagu <fd_inheritance>`, "
":meth:`~socket.socket.get_inheritable` a "
":meth:`~socket.socket.set_inheritable`."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1398
msgid ""
"The ``socket.AF_*`` and ``socket.SOCK_*`` constants are now enumeration "
"values using the new :mod:`enum` module.  This allows meaningful names to be"
" printed during debugging, instead of integer \"magic numbers\"."
msgstr ""
"Konstanty ``socket.AF_*`` a ``socket.SOCK_*`` jsou nyní vypocet hodnoty "
"pomoci noveho modulu :mod:`enum`. To umoznuje smysluplne jmena byt "
"vytisknuty pri ladeni, místo cele-cislo \"magickych cisel\"."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1402
msgid "The :const:`~socket.AF_LINK` constant is now available on BSD and OSX."
msgstr "Konstanta :const:`~socket.AF_LINK` je nyní dostupna na BSD a OSX."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1404
msgid ""
":func:`~socket.inet_pton` and :func:`~socket.inet_ntop` are now supported on"
" Windows.  (Contributed by Atsuo Ishimoto in :issue:`7171`.)"
msgstr ""
":func:`~socket.inet_pton` a :func:`~socket.inet_ntop` jsou nyní podporovany "
"na Windows. (Prispel Atsuo Ishimoto v :issue:`7171`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1409
msgid "sqlite3"
msgstr "sqlite3"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1411
msgid ""
"A new boolean parameter to the :func:`~sqlite3.connect` function, *uri*, can"
" be used to indicate that the *database* parameter is a ``uri`` (see the "
"`SQLite URI documentation <https://www.sqlite.org/uri.html>`_).  "
"(Contributed by poq in :issue:`13773`.)"
msgstr ""
"Nový boolean parametr funkce :func:`~sqlite3.connect`, *uri*, lze pouzit k "
"indikaci, ze parametr *database* je ``uri`` (viz `SQLite URI documentation "
"<https://www.sqlite.org/uri.html>`_). (Prispel poq v :issue:`13773`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1418
msgid "ssl"
msgstr "ssl"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1422
msgid ""
":data:`~ssl.PROTOCOL_TLSv1_1` and :data:`~ssl.PROTOCOL_TLSv1_2` (TLSv1.1 and"
" TLSv1.2 support) have been added; support for these protocols is only "
"available if Python is linked with OpenSSL 1.0.1 or later.  (Contributed by "
"Michele Orrù and Antoine Pitrou in :issue:`16692`.)"
msgstr ""
":data:`~ssl.PROTOCOL_TLSv1_1` a :data:`~ssl.PROTOCOL_TLSv1_2` (TLSv1.1 a "
"TLSv1.2 podpora) byly pridan; podporu pro tyto protokoly je dostupna pouze "
"pokud je Python propojen s OpenSSL 1.0.1 nebo novejsi. (Prispeli Michele "
"Orru a Antoine Pitrou v :issue:`16692`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1429
msgid ""
"New function :func:`~ssl.create_default_context` provides a standard way to "
"obtain an :class:`~ssl.SSLContext` whose settings are intended to be a "
"reasonable balance between compatibility and security.  These settings are "
"more stringent than the defaults provided by the :class:`~ssl.SSLContext` "
"constructor, and may be adjusted in the future, without prior deprecation, "
"if best-practice security requirements change.  The new recommended best "
"practice for using stdlib libraries that support SSL is to use "
":func:`~ssl.create_default_context` to obtain an :class:`~ssl.SSLContext` "
"object, modify it if needed, and then pass it as the *context* argument of "
"the appropriate stdlib API.  (Contributed by Christian Heimes in "
":issue:`19689`.)"
msgstr ""
"Nova funkce :func:`~ssl.create_default_context` poskytuje standardni způsob "
"k záskání :class:`~ssl.SSLContext` jeho nastavení je zamysleno být rozumnou "
"rovnováhou mezi kompatibilitou a bezpečností. Tato nastavení jsou prisěnější"
" než výchozí hodnoty poskytnút konstruktorem :class:`~ssl.SSLContext` a "
"mohou být upravené v budoucnosti, bez předchozí deprecace, pokud se změní "
"bezpečnostní požadavky nejlepší praxe. Nové doporučené nejlepší praxe pro "
"použití stdlib knihoven, které podporují SSL je použítí "
":func:`~ssl.create_default_context` k získání objektu "
":class:`~ssl.SSLContext`, její úpravu v případě potřeby a poté jej předáte "
"jako argument *context* vhodného API stdlib. (Prispel Christian Heimes v "
":issue:`19689`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1441
msgid ""
":class:`~ssl.SSLContext` method "
":meth:`~ssl.SSLContext.load_verify_locations` accepts a new optional "
"argument *cadata*, which can be used to provide PEM or DER encoded "
"certificates directly via strings or bytes, respectively. (Contributed by "
"Christian Heimes in :issue:`18138`.)"
msgstr ""
"Metoda :class:`~ssl.SSLContext` "
":meth:`~ssl.SSLContext.load_verify_locations` přijímá nový volitelný "
"argument *cadata*, který lze použít k poskytnutí certifikátů kódovaných PEM "
"nebo DER přímo prostřednictvím řetězců nebo bytů, v tom pořadí. (Prispel "
"Christian Heimes v :issue:`18138`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1446
msgid ""
"New function :func:`~ssl.get_default_verify_paths` returns a named tuple of "
"the paths and environment variables that the "
":meth:`~ssl.SSLContext.set_default_verify_paths` method uses to set "
"OpenSSL's default ``cafile`` and ``capath``.  This can be an aid in "
"debugging default verification issues.  (Contributed by Christian Heimes in "
":issue:`18143`.)"
msgstr ""
"Nova funkce :func:`~ssl.get_default_verify_paths` vraci pojmenovanou n-tici "
"cest a promennychannotate, ktere "
":meth:`~ssl.SSLContext.set_default_verify_paths` metoda pouziva k nastaveni "
"OpenSSL vychozi ``cafile`` a ``capath``. To muze byt pomoci pri ladeni "
"standardnich problemu s overenim. (Prispel Christian Heimes v "
":issue:`18143`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1453
msgid ""
":class:`~ssl.SSLContext` has a new method, "
":meth:`~ssl.SSLContext.cert_store_stats`, that reports the number of loaded "
"``X.509`` certs, ``X.509 CA`` certs, and certificate revocation lists "
"(``crl``\\ s), as well as a :meth:`~ssl.SSLContext.get_ca_certs` method that"
" returns a list of the loaded ``CA`` certificates.  (Contributed by "
"Christian Heimes in :issue:`18147`.)"
msgstr ""
":class:`~ssl.SSLContext` ma novou metodu, "
":meth:`~ssl.SSLContext.cert_store_stats`, ktera hlasi pocet nactenych "
"``X.509`` certs, ``X.509 CA`` certs a seznamu odvolanycertifikatu (``crl``\\"
" s), stejne jako :meth:`~ssl.SSLContext.get_ca_certs` metoda, ktera vraci "
"seznam nactenych ``CA`` certifikatu. (Prispel Christian Heimes v "
":issue:`18147`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1460
msgid ""
"If OpenSSL 0.9.8 or later is available, :class:`~ssl.SSLContext` has a new "
"attribute :attr:`~ssl.SSLContext.verify_flags` that can be used to control "
"the certificate verification process by setting it to some combination of "
"the new constants :const:`~ssl.VERIFY_DEFAULT`, "
":const:`~ssl.VERIFY_CRL_CHECK_LEAF`, :const:`~ssl.VERIFY_CRL_CHECK_CHAIN`, "
"or :const:`~ssl.VERIFY_X509_STRICT`. OpenSSL does not do any CRL "
"verification by default.  (Contributed by Christien Heimes in "
":issue:`8813`.)"
msgstr ""
"Pokud je OpenSSL 0.9.8 nebo novejsi dostupna, :class:`~ssl.SSLContext` ma "
"novy atribut :attr:`~ssl.SSLContext.verify_flags`, ktery lze pouzit pro "
"kontrolu verifikace certifikatu jeho nastavenim na nektere kombinace novych "
"konstant :const:`~ssl.VERIFY_DEFAULT`, :const:`~ssl.VERIFY_CRL_CHECK_LEAF`, "
":const:`~ssl.VERIFY_CRL_CHECK_CHAIN` nebo :const:`~ssl.VERIFY_X509_STRICT`. "
"OpenSSL nedelava vychozi zadne CRL overeni. (Prispel Christien Heimes v "
":issue:`8813`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1468
msgid ""
"New :class:`~ssl.SSLContext` method "
":meth:`~ssl.SSLContext.load_default_certs` loads a set of default "
"\"certificate authority\" (CA) certificates from default locations, which "
"vary according to the platform.  It can be used to load both TLS web server "
"authentication certificates (``purpose=``:data:`~ssl.Purpose.SERVER_AUTH`) "
"for a client to use to verify a server, and certificates for a server to use"
" in verifying client certificates "
"(``purpose=``:data:`~ssl.Purpose.CLIENT_AUTH`).  (Contributed by Christian "
"Heimes in :issue:`19292`.)"
msgstr ""
"Nova metoda :class:`~ssl.SSLContext` "
":meth:`~ssl.SSLContext.load_default_certs` nacita sadu vychozich \"certifica"
" autority\" (CA) certifikatu z vychozich mist, ktere se lisii podle "
"platformy. Lze ji pouzit k nacteni jak autentizacnich certifikatu TLS "
"weboveho serveru (``purpose=``:data:`~ssl.Purpose.SERVER_AUTH`) pro klienta "
"pouzivat k overeni serveru, tak certifikatu pro server pouzivat v overovani "
"klicenskych certifikatu (``purpose=``:data:`~ssl.Purpose.CLIENT_AUTH`). "
"(Prispel Christian Heimes v :issue:`19292`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1479
msgid ""
"Two new windows-only functions, :func:`~ssl.enum_certificates` and "
":func:`~ssl.enum_crls` provide the ability to retrieve certificates, "
"certificate information, and CRLs from the Windows cert store.  (Contributed"
" by Christian Heimes in :issue:`17134`.)"
msgstr ""
"Dve nove windows-only funkce, :func:`~ssl.enum_certificates` a "
":func:`~ssl.enum_crls` poskytuji moznost ziskat certifikaty, informace o "
"certifikatu a CRLs z Windows cert store. (Prispel Christian Heimes v "
":issue:`17134`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1486
msgid ""
"Support for server-side SNI (Server Name Indication) using the new "
":meth:`ssl.SSLContext.set_servername_callback` method. (Contributed by "
"Daniel Black in :issue:`8109`.)"
msgstr ""
"Podpora pro SNI na strane serveru (Server Name Indication) pouzitim nove "
"metody :meth:`ssl.SSLContext.set_servername_callback`. (Prispel Daniel Black"
" v :issue:`8109`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1490
msgid ""
"The dictionary returned by :meth:`.SSLSocket.getpeercert` contains "
"additional ``X509v3`` extension items: ``crlDistributionPoints``, "
"``calIssuers``, and ``OCSP`` URIs.  (Contributed by Christian Heimes in "
":issue:`18379`.)"
msgstr ""
"Slovnik vracenyvec :meth:`.SSLSocket.getpeercert` obsahuje dalsi ``X509v3`` "
"rozsirovaci polozky: ``crlDistributionPoints``, ``calIssuers` a ``OCSP`` "
"URIs. (Prispel Christian Heimes v :issue:`18379`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1496
msgid "stat"
msgstr "stat"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1498
msgid ""
"The :mod:`stat` module is now backed by a C implementation in :mod:`!_stat`."
" A C implementation is required as most of the values aren't standardized "
"and are platform-dependent.  (Contributed by Christian Heimes in "
":issue:`11016`.)"
msgstr ""
"Modul :mod:`stat` je nyní podpokojen C implementaci v :mod:`!_stat`. C "
"implementace je vyznamnana, jak vets vsech hodnot neni standardizovana a "
"jsou zavisle na platforme. (Prispel Christian Heimes v :issue:`11016`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1502
msgid ""
"The module supports new :mod:`~stat.ST_MODE` flags, :mod:`~stat.S_IFDOOR`, "
":const:`~stat.S_IFPORT`, and :const:`~stat.S_IFWHT`.  (Contributed by "
"Christian Hiemes in :issue:`11016`.)"
msgstr ""
"Modul podporuje nove :mod:`~stat.ST_MODE` priznaky, :mod:`~stat.S_IFDOOR`, "
":const:`~stat.S_IFPORT` a :const:`~stat.S_IFWHT`. (Prispel Christian Hiemes "
"v :issue:`11016`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1508
msgid "struct"
msgstr "struct"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1510
msgid ""
"New function :mod:`~struct.iter_unpack` and a new "
":meth:`struct.Struct.iter_unpack` method on compiled formats provide "
"streamed unpacking of a buffer containing repeated instances of a given "
"format of data. (Contributed by Antoine Pitrou in :issue:`17804`.)"
msgstr ""
"Nova funkce :mod:`~struct.iter_unpack` a nova metoda "
":meth:`struct.Struct.iter_unpack` na skompilovanem formatu poskytuje "
"streamovane rozbaleni bufferu obsahujiciho opakujici se instance daneho "
"formatu dat. (Prispel Antoine Pitrou v :issue:`17804`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1517
msgid "subprocess"
msgstr "subprocess"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1519
msgid ""
":func:`~subprocess.check_output` now accepts an *input* argument that can be"
" used to provide the contents of ``stdin`` for the command that is run. "
"(Contributed by Zack Weinberg in :issue:`16624`.)"
msgstr ""
":func:`~subprocess.check_output` nyní prijima argument *input*, ktery lze "
"pouzit k poskytnutiu obsahu ``stdin`` prikazu, ktery je spusten. (Prispel "
"Zack Weinberg v :issue:`16624`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1523
msgid ""
":func:`~subprocess.getoutput` and :func:`~subprocess.getstatusoutput` now "
"work on Windows.  This change was actually inadvertently made in 3.3.4. "
"(Contributed by Tim Golden in :issue:`10197`.)"
msgstr ""
":func:`~subprocess.getoutput` a :func:`~subprocess.getstatusoutput` nyní "
"pracuji na Windows. Tato zmena byla ve skutecnosti omylem provede na 3.3.4. "
"(Prispel Tim Golden v :issue:`10197`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1529
msgid "sunau"
msgstr "sunau"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1531
msgid ""
"The :meth:`!getparams` method now returns a namedtuple rather than a plain "
"tuple.  (Contributed by Claudiu Popa in :issue:`18901`.)"
msgstr ""
"Metoda :meth:`!getparams` nyní vraci pojmenovanou n-tici míste obycejne "
"n-tice. (Prispel Claudiu Popa v :issue:`18901`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1534
msgid ""
":meth:`!sunau.open` now supports the context management protocol: when used "
"in a :keyword:`with` block, the ``close`` method of the returned object will"
" be called automatically at the end of the block.  (Contributed by Serhiy "
"Storchaka in :issue:`18878`.)"
msgstr ""
":meth:`!sunau.open` nyní podporuje protokol sprav kontextu: je-li pouzito v "
":keyword:`with` bloku, bude metoda ``close`` vráceného objektu volána "
"automaticky na konci bloku. (Prispel Serhiy Storchaka v :issue:`18878`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1539
msgid ""
":meth:`!AU_write.setsampwidth` now supports 24 bit samples, thus adding "
"support for writing 24 sample using the module.  (Contributed by Serhiy "
"Storchaka in :issue:`19261`.)"
msgstr ""
":meth:`!AU_write.setsampwidth` nyní podporuje 24 bitove vzorky, tim přidaná "
"podporu pro zapis 24 vzorky použitím modulu. (Prispel Serhiy Storchaka v "
":issue:`19261`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1549
msgid "sys"
msgstr "sys"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1551
msgid ""
"New function :func:`sys.getallocatedblocks` returns the current number of "
"blocks allocated by the interpreter.  (In CPython with the default ``--with-"
"pymalloc`` setting, this is allocations made through the "
":c:func:`PyObject_Malloc` API.)  This can be useful for tracking memory "
"leaks, especially if automated via a test suite.  (Contributed by Antoine "
"Pitrou in :issue:`13390`.)"
msgstr ""
"Nova funkce :func:`sys.getallocatedblocks` vraci aktualni pocet bloku "
"alokovanych interpretem. (V CPythonu s vychozim ``--with-pymalloc`` "
"nastavenim, toto jsou alokace provedene pomoci :c:func:`PyObject_Malloc` "
"API.) To muze byt uzitecne pro sledovani netesnosti pameti, obzvlaste pokud "
"je automatizovano prostrednictvim test suite. (Prispel Antoine Pitrou v "
":issue:`13390`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1558
msgid ""
"When the Python interpreter starts in :ref:`interactive mode <tut-"
"interactive>`, it checks for an :data:`~sys.__interactivehook__` attribute "
"on the :mod:`sys` module.  If the attribute exists, its value is called with"
" no arguments just before interactive mode is started.  The check is made "
"after the :envvar:`PYTHONSTARTUP` file is read, so it can be set there.  The"
" :mod:`site` module :ref:`sets it <rlcompleter-config>` to a function that "
"enables tab completion and history saving (in :file:`~/.python-history`) if "
"the platform supports :mod:`readline`.  If you do not want this (new) "
"behavior, you can override it in :envvar:`PYTHONSTARTUP`, "
":mod:`sitecustomize`, or :mod:`usercustomize` by deleting this attribute "
"from :mod:`sys` (or setting it to some other callable).  (Contributed by "
"Éric Araujo and Antoine Pitrou in :issue:`5845`.)"
msgstr ""
"Kdyz Python interpertuje zacina v :ref:`interactive mode <tut-interactive>`,"
" zkontroluje atribut :data:`~sys.__interactivehook__` v modulu :mod:`sys`. "
"Pokud atribut existuje, jeho hodnota je volána bez argumentu pozde pred "
"interaktivnim rezimem je spusten. Kontrola je provedena po cteni souboru "
":envvar:`PYTHONSTARTUP`, takze ji muze byt nastaven tam. Modul :mod:`site` "
":ref:`je nastavuje <rlcompleter-config>` na funkci, ktera umoznuje tab "
"dokoncovani a historii ukladani (v :file:`~/.python-history`) pokud "
"platforma podporuje :mod:`readline`. Pokud nechcete toto (nove) chovani, "
"muzte jej prepsat v :envvar:`PYTHONSTARTUP`, :mod:`sitecustomize` nebo "
":mod:`usercustomize` mazanim tohoto atributu z :mod:`sys` (nebo jeho "
"nastavenim na jiny callable). (Prispeli Eric Araujo a Antoine Pitrou v "
":issue:`5845`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1573
msgid "tarfile"
msgstr "tarfile"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1575
msgid ""
"The :mod:`tarfile` module now supports a simple :ref:`tarfile-commandline` "
"when called as a script directly or via ``-m``.  This can be used to create "
"and extract tarfile archives.  (Contributed by Berker Peksag in "
":issue:`13477`.)"
msgstr ""
"Modul :mod:`tarfile` nyní podporuje jednoduchy :ref:`tarfile-commandline` "
"kdyz je volan jako skript primo nebo pomoci ``-m``. To lze pouzit k "
"vytvoreni a extrahovani tarfile archivu. (Prispel Berker Peksag v "
":issue:`13477`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1581
msgid "textwrap"
msgstr "textwrap"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1583
msgid ""
"The :class:`~textwrap.TextWrapper` class has two new attributes/constructor "
"arguments: :attr:`~textwrap.TextWrapper.max_lines`, which limits the number "
"of lines in the output, and :attr:`~textwrap.TextWrapper.placeholder`, which"
" is a string that will appear at the end of the output if it has been "
"truncated because of *max_lines*.  Building on these capabilities, a new "
"convenience function :func:`~textwrap.shorten` collapses all of the "
"whitespace in the input to single spaces and produces a single line of a "
"given *width* that ends with the *placeholder* (by default, ``[...]``).  "
"(Contributed by Antoine Pitrou and Serhiy Storchaka in :issue:`18585` and "
":issue:`18725`.)"
msgstr ""
"Trida :class:`~textwrap.TextWrapper` ma dva nove atributy/konstruktor "
"argumenty: :attr:`~textwrap.TextWrapper.max_lines`, ktery limituje pocet "
"radku na vystupu, a :attr:`~textwrap.TextWrapper.placeholder`, ktery je "
"retezec, ktery se objevuje na konci vystupu pokud byl zkracen vzhledem "
"*max_lines*. Stavajici na tychto moznostech, nova funkce pohodli "
":func:`~textwrap.shorten` sbaluje vsechny bily prostor na vstupu do "
"jednotlivych mezery a vyrabi jednoradkovy vystup dane *width*, ktery konci "
"*placeholder* (vychozi, ``[...]``). (Prispeli Antoine Pitrou a Serhiy "
"Storchaka v :issue:`18585` a :issue:`18725`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1595
msgid "threading"
msgstr "threading"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1597
msgid ""
"The :class:`~threading.Thread` object representing the main thread can be "
"obtained from the new :func:`~threading.main_thread` function.  In normal "
"conditions this will be the thread from which the Python interpreter was "
"started.  (Contributed by Andrew Svetlov in :issue:`18882`.)"
msgstr ""
"Objekt :class:`~threading.Thread` reprezentujici hlavni vlakno lze ziskat z "
"nove funkce :func:`~threading.main_thread`. V normalnih podminkach to bude "
"vlakno, ze ktereho byl interpret Python spusten. (Prispel Andrew Svetlov v "
":issue:`18882`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1604
msgid "traceback"
msgstr "traceback"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1606
msgid ""
"A new :func:`traceback.clear_frames` function takes a traceback object and "
"clears the local variables in all of the frames it references, reducing the "
"amount of memory consumed.  (Contributed by Andrew Kuchling in "
":issue:`1565525`.)"
msgstr ""
"Nova funkce :func:`traceback.clear_frames` bere objekt traceback a vycisti "
"lokalni promenne ve vsech ramcich, na ktere se odkazuje, cimz se snizuje "
"mnozstvi spolecne pameti. (Prispel Andrew Kuchling v :issue:`1565525`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1613
msgid "types"
msgstr "types"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1615
msgid ""
"A new :func:`~types.DynamicClassAttribute` descriptor provides a way to "
"define an attribute that acts normally when looked up through an instance "
"object, but which is routed to the *class* ``__getattr__`` when looked up "
"through the class.  This allows one to have properties active on a class, "
"and have virtual attributes on the class with the same name (see :mod:`enum`"
" for an example). (Contributed by Ethan Furman in :issue:`19030`.)"
msgstr ""
"Novy deskriptor :func:`~types.DynamicClassAttribute` poskytuje způsob, jak "
"definovat atribut, ktery funguje normalne pri vyhledavani prostrednictvim "
"objektu instance, ale ktery je veden na *class* ``__getattr__`` kdyz je "
"vyhledavan prostrednictvim tridy. To umoznuje mit vlastnosti aktivni v tride"
" a mit virtualni atributy v tride se stejnym jmenem (viz :mod:`enum` pro "
"priklad). (Prispel Ethan Furman v :issue:`19030`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1624
msgid "urllib"
msgstr "urllib"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1626
msgid ""
":mod:`urllib.request` now supports ``data:`` URLs via the "
":class:`~urllib.request.DataHandler` class.  (Contributed by Mathias "
"Panzenböck in :issue:`16423`.)"
msgstr ""
":mod:`urllib.request` nyní podporuje ``data:`` URLs prostrednictvim tridy "
":class:`~urllib.request.DataHandler`. (Prispel Mathias Panzenboeck v "
":issue:`16423`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1630
msgid ""
"The http method that will be used by a :class:`~urllib.request.Request` "
"class can now be specified by setting a "
":class:`~urllib.request.Request.method` class attribute on the subclass.  "
"(Contributed by Jason R Coombs in :issue:`18978`.)"
msgstr ""
"HTTP metoda, ktera bude pouzita tridou :class:`~urllib.request.Request`, "
"muze byt nyní specifikovana nastavenim atributu "
":class:`~urllib.request.Request.method` v podtride. (Prispel Jason R Coombs "
"v :issue:`18978`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1635
msgid ""
":class:`~urllib.request.Request` objects are now reusable: if the "
":attr:`~urllib.request.Request.full_url` or "
":attr:`~urllib.request.Request.data` attributes are modified, all relevant "
"internal properties are updated.  This means, for example, that it is now "
"possible to use the same :class:`~urllib.request.Request` object in more "
"than one :meth:`.OpenerDirector.open` call with different *data* arguments, "
"or to modify a :class:`~urllib.request.Request`\\ 's ``url`` rather than "
"recomputing it from scratch.  There is also a new "
":meth:`~urllib.request.Request.remove_header` method that can be used to "
"remove headers from a :class:`~urllib.request.Request`.  (Contributed by "
"Alexey Kachayev in :issue:`16464`, Daniel Wozniak in :issue:`17485`, and "
"Damien Brecht and Senthil Kumaran in :issue:`17272`.)"
msgstr ""
"Objekty :class:`~urllib.request.Request` jsou nyní znovu pouzitelne: pokud "
"jsou atributy :attr:`~urllib.request.Request.full_url` nebo "
":attr:`~urllib.request.Request.data` upraveny, jsou aktualizovany vse "
"relevantni vnitrni vlastnosti. To znamena, napríklad, ze je nyní mozne "
"pouzit stejny objekt :class:`~urllib.request.Request` vice nez jedno volani "
":meth:`.OpenerDirector.open` s ruznymi argumenty *data*, nebo upravit "
":class:`~urllib.request.Request`\\ 's ``url`` míste jeho prepocitani od "
"zacatku. Je zde take nova metoda "
":meth:`~urllib.request.Request.remove_header`, ktera muze byt pouzita k "
"odstraneni zahlavi z :class:`~urllib.request.Request`. (Prispeli Alexey "
"Kachayev v :issue:`16464`, Daniel Wozniak v :issue:`17485` a Damien Brecht a"
" Senthil Kumaran v :issue:`17272`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1648
msgid ""
":class:`~urllib.error.HTTPError` objects now have a "
":attr:`~urllib.error.HTTPError.headers` attribute that provides access to "
"the HTTP response headers associated with the error.  (Contributed by Berker"
" Peksag in :issue:`15701`.)"
msgstr ""
"Objekty :class:`~urllib.error.HTTPError` nyní mají atribut "
":attr:`~urllib.error.HTTPError.headers`, který poskytuje pristup k HTTP "
"hlavicám odezvy spojenym s chybou. (Prispel Berker Peksag v :issue:`15701`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1655
msgid "unittest"
msgstr "unittest"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1657
msgid ""
"The :class:`~unittest.TestCase` class has a new method, "
":meth:`~unittest.TestCase.subTest`, that produces a context manager whose "
":keyword:`with` block becomes a \"sub-test\".  This context manager allows a"
" test method to dynamically generate subtests  by, say, calling the "
"``subTest`` context manager inside a loop.  A single test method can thereby"
" produce an indefinite number of separately identified and separately "
"counted tests, all of which will run even if one or more of them fail.  For "
"example::"
msgstr ""
"Trida :class:`~unittest.TestCase` má novou metodu, "
":meth:`~unittest.TestCase.subTest`, ktera vyrabi spravce kontextu jehoz "
":keyword:`with` blok se stava \"pod-testem\". Tento spravce kontextu "
"umoznuje metode testu dynamicky generovat podtesty pomoci, napriklad, volaní"
" spravce ``subTest`` kontextu uvnitr smycky. Jednotliva metoda testu muze "
"tedy vyrabet neomezeny pocet oddelene identifikovanych a oddelene pocitanych"
" testu, z nichz vsechny se spusti i kdyz se jeden nebo vice z nich nezda. "
"Napríklad::"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1665
msgid ""
"class NumbersTest(unittest.TestCase):\n"
"    def test_even(self):\n"
"        for i in range(6):\n"
"            with self.subTest(i=i):\n"
"                self.assertEqual(i % 2, 0)"
msgstr ""
"class NumbersTest(unittest.TestCase):\n"
"    def test_even(self):\n"
"        for i in range(6):\n"
"            with self.subTest(i=i):\n"
"                self.assertEqual(i % 2, 0)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1671
msgid ""
"will result in six subtests, each identified in the unittest verbose output "
"with a label consisting of the variable name ``i`` and a particular value "
"for that variable (``i=0``, ``i=1``, etc).  See :ref:`subtests` for the full"
" version of this example.  (Contributed by Antoine Pitrou in "
":issue:`16997`.)"
msgstr ""
"bude vysledkem sest podtests, kazdy identifikovany v unittest verboze "
"vystupu s etiketou obsahujici nazev promenne ``i`` a konkretni hodnota pro "
"tuto promennou (``i=0``, ``i=1`` atd.). Viz :ref:`subtests` pro plnou verzi "
"tohoto příkladu. (Prispel Antoine Pitrou v :issue:`16997`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1676
msgid ""
":func:`unittest.main` now accepts an iterable of test names for "
"*defaultTest*, where previously it only accepted a single test name as a "
"string.  (Contributed by Jyrki Pulliainen in :issue:`15132`.)"
msgstr ""
":func:`unittest.main` nyní prijima iterable testu jmen pro *defaultTest*, "
"kde drive prijimala pouze jeden test jmeno jako retezec. (Prispel Jyrki "
"Pulliainen v :issue:`15132`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1680
msgid ""
"If :class:`~unittest.SkipTest` is raised during test discovery (that is, at "
"the module level in the test file), it is now reported as a skip instead of "
"an error.  (Contributed by Zach Ware in :issue:`16935`.)"
msgstr ""
"Je-li :class:`~unittest.SkipTest` vyvola behem objevu testu (tj. na urovni "
"modulu v souboru testu), je nyní hlasena jako skip namiste chyby. (Prispel "
"Zach Ware v :issue:`16935`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1684
msgid ""
":meth:`~unittest.TestLoader.discover` now sorts the discovered files to "
"provide consistent test ordering.  (Contributed by Martin Melin and Jeff "
"Ramnani in :issue:`16709`.)"
msgstr ""
":meth:`~unittest.TestLoader.discover` nyní tridi objevene soubory k "
"poskytovani konzistentnich test ustavu. (Prispeli Martin Melin a Jeff "
"Ramnani v :issue:`16709`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1688
msgid ""
":class:`~unittest.TestSuite` now drops references to tests as soon as the "
"test has been run, if the test is successful.  On Python interpreters that "
"do garbage collection, this allows the tests to be garbage collected if "
"nothing else is holding a reference to the test.  It is possible to override"
" this behavior by creating a :class:`~unittest.TestSuite` subclass that "
"defines a custom ``_removeTestAtIndex`` method.  (Contributed by Tom "
"Wardill, Matt McClure, and Andrew Svetlov in :issue:`11798`.)"
msgstr ""
":class:`~unittest.TestSuite` nyní pusti odkazy na testy hned jak test byl "
"spusten, pokud je test uspesny. Na interpretéch Pythonu, které provadějí "
"sberání odpadu, to umožnňuje testy být sebrany pokud nez nic jineho neme "
"odkaz na test. Je mozne prepisovat toto chování vytvořením "
":class:`~unittest.TestSuite` podtridy, která definuje vlastni "
"``_removeTestAtIndex`` metoda. (Prispeli Tom Wardill, Matt McClure a Andrew "
"Svetlov v :issue:`11798`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1696
msgid ""
"A new test assertion context-manager, :meth:`~unittest.TestCase.assertLogs`,"
" will ensure that a given block of code emits a log message using the "
":mod:`logging` module.  By default the message can come from any logger and "
"have a priority of ``INFO`` or higher, but both the logger name and an "
"alternative minimum logging level may be specified.  The object returned by "
"the context manager can be queried for the :class:`~logging.LogRecord`\\ s "
"and/or formatted messages that were logged.  (Contributed by Antoine Pitrou "
"in :issue:`18937`.)"
msgstr ""
"Nové test aserce kontext-spravce, :meth:`~unittest.TestCase.assertLogs`, "
"zajisti, ze daný blok kodu emituje log zprávu pomoci modulu :mod:`logging`. "
"Ve výchozím nastavení muze zpráva pocházet z jakekoli registrace a mát "
"prioritu ``INFO`` nebo vyšší, ale jak registr jméno a alternativni minimální"
" logávací úroveň mohou být specifikovány. Objekt vrácený spravcem kontextu "
"muze být dotazován na :class:`~logging.LogRecord`\\ s a/nebo formované "
"zprávy, které byly zaznamenány. (Prispel Antoine Pitrou v :issue:`18937`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1705
msgid ""
"Test discovery now works with namespace packages (Contributed by Claudiu "
"Popa in :issue:`17457`.)"
msgstr ""
"Objevování testu nyní pracuje s namespace balicky (Prispel Claudiu Popa v "
":issue:`17457`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1708
msgid ""
":mod:`unittest.mock` objects now inspect their specification signatures when"
" matching calls, which means an argument can now be matched by either "
"position or name, instead of only by position.  (Contributed by Antoine "
"Pitrou in :issue:`17015`.)"
msgstr ""
"Objekty :mod:`unittest.mock` nyní inspektor jejich specifikace podpisy pri "
"shodování volání, coz znamena, ze argument muze být nyní shoden buď podle "
"pozice nebo jména, místo pouze podle pozice. (Prispel Antoine Pitrou v "
":issue:`17015`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1713
msgid ""
":func:`~unittest.mock.mock_open` objects now have ``readline`` and "
"``readlines`` methods.  (Contributed by Toshio Kuratomi in :issue:`17467`.)"
msgstr ""
"Objekty :func:`~unittest.mock.mock_open` nyní mají metody ``readline`` a "
"``readlines``. (Prispel Toshio Kuratomi v :issue:`17467`.)"

