"Parametr *allowZip64* pro :class:`~zipfile.ZipFile` a "
":class:`~zipfile.PyZipFile` je nyní ``True`` ve výchozím nastavení. (Prispel"
" William Mallard v :issue:`17201`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1798
msgid "CPython Implementation Changes"
msgstr "Zmeny implementace CPython"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1804
msgid "PEP 445: Customization of CPython Memory Allocators"
msgstr "PEP 445: Customizace alokátorů paměti CPython"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1806
msgid ""
":pep:`445` adds new C level interfaces to customize memory allocation in the"
" CPython interpreter."
msgstr ""
":pep:`445` pridava nova rozhrani na urovni C k customize alokace pameti v "
"interpretu CPython."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1811
msgid ":pep:`445` -- Add new APIs to customize Python memory allocators"
msgstr ":pep:`445` -- Pridej nove API k customize alokaci pameti Python"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1818
msgid "PEP 442: Safe Object Finalization"
msgstr "PEP 442: Bezpecne dokoncení objektu"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1820
msgid ""
":pep:`442` removes the current limitations and quirks of object finalization"
" in CPython. With it, objects with :meth:`~object.__del__` methods, as well "
"as generators with :keyword:`finally` clauses, can be finalized when they "
"are part of a reference cycle."
msgstr ""
":pep:`442` odstranjó aktuální omezení a zvláštnosti finalizace objektu v "
"CPython. S tím, objekty s metodami :meth:`~object.__del__`, stejně jako "
"generátory s klauzulemi :keyword:`finally`, mohou být finalizovány, když "
"jsou součástí cyklu odkazu."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1825
msgid ""
"As part of this change, module globals are no longer forcibly set to "
":const:`None` during interpreter shutdown in most cases, instead relying on "
"the normal operation of the cyclic garbage collector.  This avoids a whole "
"class of interpreter-shutdown-time errors, usually involving ``__del__`` "
"methods, that have plagued Python since the cyclic GC was first introduced."
msgstr ""
"Jako soucast teto zmeny, modul globaly jsou jiz ne vynucenym nastavenim na "
":const:`None` behem vypnuti interpretru ve vetsine pripadu, namiste "
"spolenuti na normalni provoz cyklickeho sberace odpadu. To se vyha cele "
"tride vypnutim-cas chyby, obvykle zahrnující ``__del__`` metody, ktery "
"prisely Python od cyklicke GC byla první predstavena."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1834
msgid ":pep:`442` -- Safe object finalization"
msgstr ":pep:`442` -- Bezpecne dokoncení objektu"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1841
msgid "PEP 456: Secure and Interchangeable Hash Algorithm"
msgstr "PEP 456: Bezpecny a vymennitelny hashovaci algoritmus"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1843
msgid ""
":pep:`456` follows up on earlier security fix work done on Python's hash "
"algorithm to address certain DOS attacks to which public facing APIs backed "
"by dictionary lookups may be subject.  (See :issue:`14621` for the start of "
"the current round of improvements.)  The PEP unifies CPython's hash code to "
"make it easier for a packager to substitute a different hash algorithm, and "
"switches Python's default implementation to a SipHash implementation on "
"platforms that have a 64 bit data type.  Any performance differences in "
"comparison with the older FNV algorithm are trivial."
msgstr ""
":pep:`456` nasleduje drivější bezpecnostní prace opravy naden na Pythonu "
"algoritmu hash k adrese certain DOS u tok, na ktere verejne celen API "
"zalozen slovnick lookup mohou být sémantika. (Viz :issue:`14621` pro zacatek"
" soucasneho kola zlepseni.) PEP sjednocuje hash kod CPython aby se usnadnil "
"zamenitele odlisneho hashovacího algoritmu a prepina Python vychozi "
"implementaci na SipHash implementaci na platformach, ktere mají 64 bit data "
"typ. Jakekoli rozdily vykonu v srovnání se starším FNV algoritmem jsou "
"trivialní."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1852
msgid ""
"The PEP adds additional fields to the :data:`sys.hash_info` named tuple to "
"describe the hash algorithm in use by the currently executing binary.  "
"Otherwise, the PEP does not alter any existing CPython APIs."
msgstr ""
"PEP prida dalsich poli do :data:`sys.hash_info` pojmenovane n-tici popsat "
"hashovaci algoritmus v pouziti v soucasne vykonanem binarni. Jinak, PEP "
"nezmeni zadny existujici API CPython."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1860
msgid "PEP 436: Argument Clinic"
msgstr "PEP 436: Argument Clinic"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1862
msgid ""
"\"Argument Clinic\" (:pep:`436`) is now part of the CPython build process "
"and can be used to simplify the process of defining and maintaining accurate"
" signatures for builtins and standard library extension modules implemented "
"in C."
msgstr ""
"\"Argument Clinic\" (:pep:`436`) je nyní součástí procesu stavby CPython a "
"muze být pouzita ke zjednoduseni procesu definovani a udrzovani presnych "
"podpisech pro vestavne a rozsirovaci moduly standardni knihovny "
"implementovane v C."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1867
msgid ""
"Some standard library extension modules have been converted to use Argument "
"Clinic in Python 3.4, and :mod:`pydoc` and :mod:`inspect` have been updated "
"accordingly."
msgstr ""
"Nektere standardni knihovny rozsirovaci moduly byly prepraveny pouzit "
"Argument Clinic v Python 3.4 a :mod:`pydoc` a :mod:`inspect` byly "
"aktualizable v souladu."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1871
msgid ""
"It is expected that signature metadata for programmatic introspection will "
"be added to additional callables implemented in C as part of Python 3.4 "
"maintenance releases."
msgstr ""
"Se ocekava, ze metadata podpisu pro programatickou introspekci budou pridany"
" do dalsich callable implementovaneho v C jako soucast Python 3.4 udrzovani "
"vydani."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1876
msgid ""
"The Argument Clinic PEP is not fully up to date with the state of the "
"implementation. This has been deemed acceptable by the release manager and "
"core development team in this case, as Argument Clinic will not be made "
"available as a public API for third party use in Python 3.4."
msgstr ""
"PEP Argument Clinic neni plne aktualni se stavem implementace. To bylo "
"vyznameno prijatelne vedoucim vydani a hlavni vyvojovy tym v tomto pripadu, "
"jako Argument Clinic nebude provedeno jako verejne API pro tretich stran "
"pouziti v Python 3.4."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1883
msgid ":pep:`436` -- The Argument Clinic DSL"
msgstr ":pep:`436` -- Argument Clinic DSL"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1884
msgid "PEP written and implemented by Larry Hastings."
msgstr "PEP napsan a implementovan Larry Hastings."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1888
msgid "Other Build and C API Changes"
msgstr "Dalsi Build a C API zmeny"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1890
msgid ""
"The new :c:func:`PyType_GetSlot` function has been added to the stable ABI, "
"allowing retrieval of function pointers from named type slots when using the"
" limited API.  (Contributed by Martin von Löwis in :issue:`17162`.)"
msgstr ""
"Nova funkce :c:func:`PyType_GetSlot` byla pridan do stabilniho ABI, umoznuje"
" ziskani pointeru funkce z pojmenovanych typu slotu pri pouziti omezenym "
"API. (Prispel Martin von Lowis v :issue:`17162`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1894
msgid ""
"The new :c:func:`!Py_SetStandardStreamEncoding` pre-initialization API "
"allows applications embedding the CPython interpreter to reliably force a "
"particular encoding and error handler for the standard streams. (Contributed"
" by Bastien Montagne and Nick Coghlan in :issue:`16129`.)"
msgstr ""
"Nova :c:func:`!Py_SetStandardStreamEncoding` pred-inicializace API umoznuje "
"aplikacim vnorovani interpretu CPython spolehlivym zpusobem vynutit "
"konkretni kodovani a spravce chyb pro standardni toky. (Prispeli Bastien "
"Montagne a Nick Coghlan v :issue:`16129`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1899
msgid ""
"Most Python C APIs that don't mutate string arguments are now correctly "
"marked as accepting ``const char *`` rather than ``char *``.  (Contributed "
"by Serhiy Storchaka in :issue:`1772673`.)"
msgstr ""
"Vetsina Python C API, ktera ne mutace argumenty retezce, jsou nyní spravne "
"oznaceny jako prijimajici ``const char *`` nez ``char *``. (Prispel Serhiy "
"Storchaka v :issue:`1772673`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1903
msgid ""
"A new shell version of ``python-config`` can be used even when a python "
"interpreter is not available (for example, in cross compilation scenarios)."
msgstr ""
"Nova shell verze ``python-config`` muze byt pouzita i kdyz python "
"interpreter neni dostupna (napríklad, v scenarech krizoveho kompilace)."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1906
#, python-format
msgid ""
":c:func:`PyUnicode_FromFormat` now supports width and precision "
"specifications for ``%s``, ``%A``, ``%U``, ``%V``, ``%S``, and ``%R``. "
"(Contributed by Ysj Ray and Victor Stinner in :issue:`7330`.)"
msgstr ""
":c:func:`PyUnicode_FromFormat` nyní podporuje sirku a presne specifikace pro"
" ``%s``, ``%A``, ``%U``, ``%V``, ``%S`` a ``%R``. (Prispeli Ysj Ray a Victor"
" Stinner v :issue:`7330`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1910
msgid ""
"New function :c:func:`PyStructSequence_InitType2` supplements the existing "
":c:func:`PyStructSequence_InitType` function.  The difference is that it "
"returns ``0`` on success and ``-1`` on failure."
msgstr ""
"Nova funkce :c:func:`PyStructSequence_InitType2` doplnuje existujici "
":c:func:`PyStructSequence_InitType` funkci. Rozdil je, ze vraci ``0`` na "
"uspech a ``-1`` na selhani."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1914
msgid ""
"The CPython source can now be compiled using the address sanity checking "
"features of recent versions of GCC and clang:  the false alarms in the small"
" object allocator have been silenced.  (Contributed by Dhiru Kholia in "
":issue:`18596`.)"
msgstr ""
"Zdrojovy kod CPython muze byt nyní kompilovan pouzitim prvku kontroly "
"samitnosti adresy nedavnych verzich GCC a clang: falesne alarmy v male "
"alokatore objektu byly utlumeny. (Prispel Dhiru Kholia v :issue:`18596`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1919
msgid ""
"The Windows build now uses `Address Space Layout Randomization "
"<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Address_space_layout_randomization>`_ and "
"`Data Execution Prevention "
"<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Data_Execution_Prevention>`_.  (Contributed "
"by Christian Heimes in :issue:`16632`.)"
msgstr ""
"Build Windows nyní pouziva `Address Space Layout Randomization "
"<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Address_space_layout_randomization>`_ a `Data"
" Execution Prevention "
"<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Data_Execution_Prevention>`_. (Prispel "
"Christian Heimes v :issue:`16632`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1924
msgid ""
"New function :c:func:`PyObject_LengthHint` is the C API equivalent of "
":func:`operator.length_hint`.  (Contributed by Armin Ronacher in "
":issue:`16148`.)"
msgstr ""
"Nova funkce :c:func:`PyObject_LengthHint` je C API ekvivalent "
":func:`operator.length_hint`. (Prispel Armin Ronacher v :issue:`16148`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1932
msgid "Other Improvements"
msgstr "Jine zlepseni"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1936
msgid ""
"The :ref:`python <using-on-cmdline>` command has a new :ref:`option <using-"
"on-misc-options>`, ``-I``, which causes it to run in \"isolated mode\", "
"which means that :data:`sys.path` contains neither the script's directory "
"nor the user's ``site-packages`` directory, and all :envvar:`!PYTHON*` "
"environment variables are ignored (it implies both ``-s`` and ``-E``).  "
"Other restrictions may also be applied in the future, with the goal being to"
" isolate the execution of a script from the user's environment.  This is "
"appropriate, for example, when Python is used to run a system script.  On "
"most POSIX systems it can and should be used in the ``#!`` line of system "
"scripts.  (Contributed by Christian Heimes in :issue:`16499`.)"
msgstr ""
"Prikaz :ref:`python <using-on-cmdline>` ma novou :ref:`moznost <using-on-"
"misc-options>`, ``-I``, ktera jej zpusob chod v \"izolovanem rezimu\", ktery"
" znamena, ze :data:`sys.path` obsahuje ani adresar skriptu ani uzivatelsky "
"``site-packages`` adresar a vsechny promenne okoli :envvar:`!PYTHON*` jsou "
"ignorovany (znamena to obe ``-s`` a ``-E``). Ostatni omezeni mohou byt "
"aplikovany v budoucnosti, s cilem je izolovat provozovani skriptu z "
"prostredi uzivatele. To je vhodne, napríklad, kdyz Python je pouzit pro "
"spusteni systemoveho skriptu. Na vetsine systemu POSIX muze a mel by byt "
"pouzit v ``#!`` radku systemovych skriptu. (Prispel Christian Heimes v "
":issue:`16499`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1947
msgid ""
"Tab-completion is now enabled by default in the interactive interpreter on "
"systems that support :mod:`readline`.  History is also enabled by default, "
"and is written to (and read from) the file :file:`~/.python-history`. "
"(Contributed by Antoine Pitrou and Éric Araujo in :issue:`5845`.)"
msgstr ""
"Tab-dokonceni je nyní povoleno ve vychozim nastaveni v interaktivnim "
"interpretu na systemech, ktere podporuji :mod:`readline`. Historie je take "
"povolena ve vychozim nastaveni a je zapsana do (a ctena z) souboru "
":file:`~/.python-history`. (Prispeli Antoine Pitrou a Eric Araujo v "
":issue:`5845`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1952
msgid ""
"Invoking the Python interpreter with ``--version`` now outputs the version "
"to standard output instead of standard error (:issue:`18338`). Similar "
"changes were made to :mod:`argparse` (:issue:`18920`) and other modules that"
" have script-like invocation capabilities (:issue:`18922`)."
msgstr ""
"Vyvolaní interpretu Python s ``--version`` nyní vyvola verzi standardniho "
"vystupu míste standardni chyby (:issue:`18338`). Podobne zmeny byly "
"provedeny v :mod:`argparse` (:issue:`18920`) a ostatnich modulech, ktere "
"mají moznosti vyvolaní podobne skriptum (:issue:`18922`)."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1957
msgid ""
"The CPython Windows installer now adds ``.py`` to the :envvar:`PATHEXT` "
"variable when extensions are registered, allowing users to run a python "
"script at the windows command prompt by just typing its name without the "
"``.py`` extension.  (Contributed by Paul Moore in :issue:`18569`.)"
msgstr ""
"Instalace CPython Windows nyní prida ``.py`` k promenne :envvar:`PATHEXT` "
"kdyz jsou rozsirenipo registrovany, umoznujici uzivatelum spustit python "
"skript na windows prikazoveho radku pouze jeho napisanim bez ``.py`` "
"pripony. (Prispel Paul Moore v :issue:`18569`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1962
msgid ""
"A new ``make`` target `coverage-report "
"<https://devguide.python.org/coverage/#measuring-coverage-of-c-code-with-"
"gcov-and-lcov>`_ will build python, run the test suite, and generate an HTML"
" coverage report for the C codebase using ``gcov`` and `lcov "
"<https://github.com/linux-test-project/lcov>`_."
msgstr ""
"Novó ``make`` cil `coverage-report "
"<https://devguide.python.org/coverage/#measuring-coverage-of-c-code-with-"
"gcov-and-lcov>`_ bude vystavba python, spustit sadu testu a generat HTML "
"zpravy pokryti pro kodex C pomoci ``gcov`` a `lcov "
"<https://github.com/linux-test-project/lcov>`_."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1968
msgid ""
"The ``-R`` option to the :ref:`python regression test suite <regrtest>` now "
"also checks for memory allocation leaks, using "
":func:`sys.getallocatedblocks`.  (Contributed by Antoine Pitrou in "
":issue:`13390`.)"
msgstr ""
"Volba ``-R`` k :ref:`python regression test suite <regrtest>` nyní take "
"kontroluje nedostatek alokace pameti, pouzitim "
":func:`sys.getallocatedblocks`. (Prispel Antoine Pitrou v :issue:`13390`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1973
msgid "``python -m`` now works with namespace packages."
msgstr "``python -m`` nyní pracuje s namespace balicky."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1975
msgid ""
"The :mod:`stat` module is now implemented in C, which means it gets the "
"values for its constants from the C header files, instead of having the "
"values hard-coded in the python module as was previously the case."
msgstr ""
"Modul :mod:`stat` je nyní implementovan v C, znamena to, ze dostane hodnoty "
"pro jeho konstanty ze C hlavickych souboru, míste nez bylo hodnoty pevne "
"kodovano v python modulu jako byla drive pripad."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1979
msgid ""
"Loading multiple python modules from a single OS module (``.so``, ``.dll``) "
"now works correctly (previously it silently returned the first python module"
" in the file).  (Contributed by Václav Šmilauer in :issue:`16421`.)"
msgstr ""
"Nacteni vice python modulu z jednoho modulu OS (``.so``, ``.dll``) nyní "
"pracuje spravne (drive se tiche vrátilo první python modul v souboru). "
"(Prispel Václav Šmilauer v :issue:`16421`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1983
msgid ""
"A new opcode, :opcode:`!LOAD_CLASSDEREF`, has been added to fix a bug in the"
" loading of free variables in class bodies that could be triggered by "
"certain uses of :ref:`__prepare__ <prepare>`.  (Contributed by Benjamin "
"Peterson in :issue:`17853`.)"
msgstr ""
"Novy opcod, :opcode:`!LOAD_CLASSDEREF`, byl pridan k oprave chyby pri "
"nacitani svobodnych promennych v tridach, ktere by mohly byt spusten "
"urcitymi pouzitim :ref:`__prepare__ <prepare>`. (Prispel Benjamin Peterson v"
" :issue:`17853`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1988
msgid ""
"A number of MemoryError-related crashes were identified and fixed by Victor "
"Stinner using his :pep:`445`-based ``pyfailmalloc`` tool (:issue:`18408`, "
":issue:`18520`)."
msgstr ""
"Pocet padi souvisejici MemoryError byly identifikovany a opraveny Victor "
"Stinner pomoci jeho :pep:`445`-zalozeneho ``pyfailmalloc`` nastroje "
"(:issue:`18408`, :issue:`18520`)."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1992
msgid ""
"The ``pyvenv`` command now accepts a ``--copies`` option to use copies "
"rather than symlinks even on systems where symlinks are the default.  "
"(Contributed by Vinay Sajip in :issue:`18807`.)"
msgstr ""
"Prikaz ``pyvenv`` nyní prijima volbu ``--copies`` pouzivat kopie nez "
"symlinky i na systemech, kde symlinky jsou vychozi. (Prispel Vinay Sajip v "
":issue:`18807`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:1996
msgid ""
"The ``pyvenv`` command also accepts a ``--without-pip`` option to suppress "
"the otherwise-automatic bootstrapping of pip into the virtual environment.  "
"(Contributed by Nick Coghlan in :issue:`19552` as part of the :pep:`453` "
"implementation.)"
msgstr ""
"Prikaz ``pyvenv`` take prijima volbu ``--without-pip`` potlacit jinak-"
"automaticke spousteni pip do virtualniho prostredi. (Prispel Nick Coghlan v "
":issue:`19552` jako soucast implementace :pep:`453`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2001
msgid ""
"The encoding name is now optional in the value set for the "
":envvar:`PYTHONIOENCODING` environment variable.  This makes it possible to "
"set just the error handler, without changing the default encoding. "
"(Contributed by Serhiy Storchaka in :issue:`18818`.)"
msgstr ""
"Nazev kodovani je nyní volitelny v hodnote nastavene pro promennou okoli "
":envvar:`PYTHONIOENCODING`. To cinni mozne nastavit jen spravce chyb, bez "
"zmeny vychozi kodovani. (Prispel Serhiy Storchaka v :issue:`18818`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2006
msgid ""
"The :mod:`bz2`, :mod:`lzma`, and :mod:`gzip` module ``open`` functions now "
"support ``x`` (exclusive creation) mode.  (Contributed by Tim Heaney and "
"Vajrasky Kok in :issue:`19201`, :issue:`19222`, and :issue:`19223`.)"
msgstr ""
"Funkce :mod:`bz2`, :mod:`lzma` a :mod:`gzip` modul ``open`` nyní podporuji "
"``x`` (eksklusivni vytvoreni) rezim. (Prispeli Tim Heaney a Vajrasky Kok v "
":issue:`19201`, :issue:`19222` a :issue:`19223`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2012
msgid "Significant Optimizations"
msgstr "Vyznamna optimalizace"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2014
msgid ""
"The UTF-32 decoder is now 3x to 4x faster.  (Contributed by Serhiy Storchaka"
" in :issue:`14625`.)"
msgstr ""
"UTF-32 dekoder je nyní 3x az 4x rychlejsi. (Prispel Serhiy Storchaka v "
":issue:`14625`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2017
msgid ""
"The cost of hash collisions for sets is now reduced.  Each hash table probe "
"now checks a series of consecutive, adjacent key/hash pairs before "
"continuing to make random probes through the hash table.  This exploits "
"cache locality to make collision resolution less expensive. The collision "
"resolution scheme can be described as a hybrid of linear probing and open "
"addressing.  The number of additional linear probes defaults to nine.  This "
"can be changed at compile-time by defining LINEAR_PROBES to be any value.  "
"Set LINEAR_PROBES=0 to turn-off linear probing entirely.  (Contributed by "
"Raymond Hettinger in :issue:`18771`.)"
msgstr ""
"Cena kolizi hashovani pro sady je nyní snizena. Kazdy prieskum tabulky "
"hashovani nyní kontroluje serii po sobe jdoucich, sousedni klucova/hash "
"dvojice pred pokracovanim provest nahodne prohledy pres tabulku hashovani. "
"To vyuziva lokalitu cache aby vyreseni kolizi bylo mene drahe. Schemat "
"vyreseni kolizi muze byt popsana jako hybrid linearniho zkuseni a otevrene "
"adrese. Pocet dalsich linearnich porob vychodchozi na devet. To muze byt "
"zmenenopri compile-time definovani LINEAR_PROBES na jakauko hodnotu. "
"Nastaveni LINEAR_PROBES=0 k vypnuti linearniho sondy zcela. (Prispel Raymond"
" Hettinger v :issue:`18771`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2028
#, no-python-format
msgid ""
"The interpreter starts about 30% faster. A couple of measures lead to the "
"speedup. The interpreter loads fewer modules on startup, e.g. the :mod:`re`,"
" :mod:`collections` and :mod:`locale` modules and their dependencies are no "
"longer imported by default. The marshal module has been improved to load "
"compiled Python code faster.  (Contributed by Antoine Pitrou, Christian "
"Heimes and Victor Stinner in :issue:`19219`, :issue:`19218`, :issue:`19209`,"
" :issue:`19205` and :issue:`9548`.)"
msgstr ""
"Interpreter se spusti asi o 30% rychleji. Paar opatreni vede ke zrychleni. "
"Interpret nacita mene modulu pri spusteni, napríklad :mod:`re`, "
":mod:`collections` a :mod:`locale` moduly a jejich zavislosti jiz nejsou "
"importovany ve vychozim nastaveni. Modul marshal byl zlepsen k nacteni "
"skompiloveho kodu Python rychleji. (Prispeli Antoine Pitrou, Christian "
"Heimes a Victor Stinner v :issue:`19219`, :issue:`19218`, :issue:`19209`, "
":issue:`19205` a :issue:`9548`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2036
msgid ""
":class:`bz2.BZ2File` is now as fast or faster than the Python2 version for "
"most cases.  :class:`lzma.LZMAFile` has also been optimized.  (Contributed "
"by Serhiy Storchaka and Nadeem Vawda in :issue:`16034`.)"
msgstr ""
":class:`bz2.BZ2File` je nyní stejne nebo rychleji nez verze Python2 pro "
"vetsinu pripadu. :class:`lzma.LZMAFile` byla take optimalizovana. (Prispeli "
"Serhiy Storchaka a Nadeem Vawda v :issue:`16034`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2040
#, no-python-format
msgid ""
":func:`random.getrandbits` is 20%-40% faster for small integers (the most "
"common use case).  (Contributed by Serhiy Storchaka in :issue:`16674`.)"
msgstr ""
":func:`random.getrandbits` je 20%-40% rychlejsi pro male cele cisla "
"(nejcastejsi pripad pouziti). (Prispel Serhiy Storchaka v :issue:`16674`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2043
msgid ""
"By taking advantage of the new storage format for strings, pickling of "
"strings is now significantly faster.  (Contributed by Victor Stinner and "
"Antoine Pitrou in :issue:`15596`.)"
msgstr ""
"Vyuzitim vychody novych uloziste pro retezce, picckling retezcu je nyní "
"vyrazne rychlejsi. (Prispeli Victor Stinner a Antoine Pitrou v "
":issue:`15596`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2047
msgid ""
"A performance issue in :meth:`!io.FileIO.readall` has been solved.  This "
"particularly affects Windows, and significantly speeds up the case of piping"
" significant amounts of data through :mod:`subprocess`.  (Contributed by "
"Richard Oudkerk in :issue:`15758`.)"
msgstr ""
"Vykon problemou v :meth:`!io.FileIO.readall` byl vyresan. To zvlaste "
"ovlivnuje Windows a vyrazne urychluje pripad pouziti trube vyznamneho objemu"
" dat pres :mod:`subprocess`. (Prispel Richard Oudkerk v :issue:`15758`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2052
msgid ""
":func:`html.escape` is now 10x faster.  (Contributed by Matt Bryant in "
":issue:`18020`.)"
msgstr ""
":func:`html.escape` je nyní 10x rychlejsi. (Prispel Matt Bryant v "
":issue:`18020`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2055
msgid ""
"On Windows, the native ``VirtualAlloc`` is now used instead of the CRT "
"``malloc`` in ``obmalloc``.  Artificial benchmarks show about a 3% memory "
"savings."
msgstr ""
"Na Windows, nativni ``VirtualAlloc`` je nyní pouzivan míste CRT ``malloc`` v"
" ``obmalloc``. Umele benchmarky ukazuji priblizne 3% uspory pameti."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2059
msgid ""
":func:`os.urandom` now uses a lazily opened persistent file descriptor so as"
" to avoid using many file descriptors when run in parallel from multiple "
"threads.  (Contributed by Antoine Pitrou in :issue:`18756`.)"
msgstr ""
":func:`os.urandom` nyní pouziva lhostejne otevreny perzistentni deskriptor "
"souboru tak aby se vyhmul pouziti mnoha deskriptorů souboru, kdyz je spusten"
" v paralelu z vice vlaken. (Prispel Antoine Pitrou v :issue:`18756`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2067
msgid "Deprecated"
msgstr "Zastarale"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2069
msgid ""
"This section covers various APIs and other features that have been "
"deprecated in Python 3.4, and will be removed in Python 3.5 or later.  In "
"most (but not all) cases, using the deprecated APIs will produce a "
":exc:`DeprecationWarning` when the interpreter is run with deprecation "
"warnings enabled (for example, by using ``-Wd``)."
msgstr ""
"Tato cast pokryva rozne API a ostatni vlastnosti, ktere byly zastarale v "
"Python 3.4 a budou odstranen v Python 3.5 nebo pozdeji. Ve vetsine (ale ne v"
" sech) pripadech, pouzivani zastaralych API bude vyprodukovat "
":exc:`DeprecationWarning` kdyz je interpret spusten s deprecation varovanim "
"povoleno (napríklad, pouzitim ``-Wd``)."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2077
msgid "Deprecations in the Python API"
msgstr "Zastaraly v Python API"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2079
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"As mentioned in :ref:`whatsnew-pep-451`, a number of :mod:`importlib` "
"methods and functions are deprecated: :meth:`!importlib.find_loader` is "
"replaced by :func:`importlib.util.find_spec`; "
":meth:`!importlib.machinery.PathFinder.find_module` is replaced by "
":meth:`importlib.machinery.PathFinder.find_spec`; "
":meth:`!importlib.abc.MetaPathFinder.find_module` is replaced by "
":meth:`importlib.abc.MetaPathFinder.find_spec`; "
":meth:`!importlib.abc.PathEntryFinder.find_loader` and :meth:`!find_module` "
"are replaced by :meth:`importlib.abc.PathEntryFinder.find_spec`; all of the "
":samp:`{xxx}Loader` ABC ``load_module`` methods "
"(:meth:`!importlib.abc.Loader.load_module`, "
":meth:`!importlib.abc.InspectLoader.load_module`, "
":meth:`!importlib.abc.FileLoader.load_module`, "
":meth:`!importlib.abc.SourceLoader.load_module`) should no longer be "
"implemented, instead loaders should implement an ``exec_module`` method "
"(:meth:`importlib.abc.Loader.exec_module`, "
":meth:`importlib.abc.InspectLoader.exec_module` "
":meth:`importlib.abc.SourceLoader.exec_module`) and let the import system "
"take care of the rest; and :meth:`!importlib.abc.Loader.module_repr`, "
":meth:`!importlib.util.module_for_loader`, "
":meth:`!importlib.util.set_loader`, and :meth:`!importlib.util.set_package` "
"are no longer needed because their functions are now handled automatically "
"by the import system."
msgstr ""
"Jak je zminneno v :ref:`whatsnew-pep-451`, pocet :mod:`importlib` metod a "
"funkci jsou zastarale: :meth:`!importlib.find_loader` je nahrazen "
":func:`importlib.util.find_spec`; "
":meth:`!importlib.machinery.PathFinder.find_module` je nahrazen "
":meth:`importlib.machinery.PathFinder.find_spec`; "
":meth:`!importlib.abc.MetaPathFinder.find_module` je nahrazen "
":meth:`importlib.abc.MetaPathFinder.find_spec`; "
":meth:`!importlib.abc.PathEntryFinder.find_loader` a :meth:`!find_module` "
"jsou nahrazeny :meth:`importlib.abc.PathEntryFinder.find_spec`; vsechny "
":samp:`{xxx}Loader` ABC ``load_module`` metody "
"(:meth:`!importlib.abc.Loader.load_module`, "
":meth:`!importlib.abc.InspectLoader.load_module`, "
":meth:`!importlib.abc.FileLoader.load_module`, "
":meth:`!importlib.abc.SourceLoader.load_module`) by jiz nemely byt "
"implementovany, miste toho by mel zatezovac implementovat ``exec_module`` "
"metodu (:meth:`importlib.abc.Loader.exec_module`, "
":meth:`importlib.abc.InspectLoader.exec_module` "
":meth:`importlib.abc.SourceLoader.exec_module`) a nechat importni system "
"starat se o zbytek; a :meth:`!importlib.abc.Loader.module_repr`, "
":meth:`!importlib.util.module_for_loader`, "
":meth:`!importlib.util.set_loader` a :meth:`!importlib.util.set_package` jiz"
" nejsou potrebne, protoze jejich funkce jsou nyní pracovany automaticky "
"importem systém."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2104
msgid ""
"The :mod:`!imp` module is pending deprecation. To keep compatibility with "
"Python 2/3 code bases, the module's removal is currently not scheduled."
msgstr ""
"Modul :mod:`!imp` ceka deprecace. Aby byla zachovana kompatibilita s kodem "
"Python 2/3, odstranímodulu se v soucasne dobe neplanu."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2107
msgid ""
"The :mod:`!formatter` module is pending deprecation and is slated for "
"removal in Python 3.6."
msgstr ""
"Modul :mod:`!formatter` ceka deprecace a je vymezen pro odstraneni v Python "
"3.6."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2110
msgid ""
"``MD5`` as the default *digestmod* for the :func:`hmac.new` function is "
"deprecated.  Python 3.6 will require an explicit digest name or constructor "
"as *digestmod* argument."
msgstr ""
"``MD5`` jako vychozi *digestmod* pro funkci :func:`hmac.new` je zastarale. "
"Python 3.6 bude vyzidat explicite jmeno digestu nebo konstruktor jako "
"argument *digestmod*."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2114
msgid ""
"The internal ``Netrc`` class in the :mod:`ftplib` module has been documented"
" as deprecated in its docstring for quite some time.  It now emits a "
":exc:`DeprecationWarning` and will be removed completely in Python 3.5."
msgstr ""
"Vnitrni trida ``Netrc`` v modulu :mod:`ftplib` byla dokumentovana jako "
"zastarale v jeji docstringu po dlouhou dobu. To nyní emituje "
":exc:`DeprecationWarning` a bude zcela odstranen v Python 3.5."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2118
msgid ""
"The undocumented *endtime* argument to :meth:`subprocess.Popen.wait` should "
"not have been exposed and is hopefully not in use; it is deprecated and will"
" mostly likely be removed in Python 3.5."
msgstr ""
"Nedokumentovany argument *endtime* na :meth:`subprocess.Popen.wait` by nemel"
" byt vystavena a doufejme, ze neni v pouziti; je zastarale a bude "
"pravdepodobne odstraneno v Python 3.5."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2122
msgid ""
"The *strict* argument of :class:`~html.parser.HTMLParser` is deprecated."
msgstr "Argument *strict* z :class:`~html.parser.HTMLParser` je zastarale."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2124
msgid ""
"The :mod:`plistlib` :func:`!readPlist`, :func:`!writePlist`, "
":func:`!readPlistFromBytes`, and :func:`!writePlistToBytes` functions are "
"deprecated in favor of the corresponding new functions "
":func:`~plistlib.load`, :func:`~plistlib.dump`, :func:`~plistlib.loads`, and"
" :func:`~plistlib.dumps`.  :func:`!Data` is deprecated in favor of just "
"using the :class:`bytes` constructor."
msgstr ""
"Funkce :mod:`plistlib` :func:`!readPlist`, :func:`!writePlist`, "
":func:`!readPlistFromBytes` a :func:`!writePlistToBytes` jsou zastarale ve "
"prospech odpovidajicich novych funkci :func:`~plistlib.load`, "
":func:`~plistlib.dump`, :func:`~plistlib.loads` a :func:`~plistlib.dumps`. "
":func:`!Data` je zastarale ve prospech pouziti pouze konstruktoru "
":class:`bytes`."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2131
msgid ""
"The :mod:`sysconfig` key ``SO`` is deprecated, it has been replaced by "
"``EXT_SUFFIX``."
msgstr ""
"Klic :mod:`sysconfig` ``SO`` je zastarale, byl nahrazen ``EXT_SUFFIX``."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2134
msgid ""
"The ``U`` mode accepted by various ``open`` functions is deprecated. In "
"Python3 it does not do anything useful, and should be replaced by "
"appropriate uses of :class:`io.TextIOWrapper` (if needed) and its *newline* "
"argument."
msgstr ""
"Rezim ``U`` prijimanym ruznyma ``open`` funkcemi je zastarale. V Python3 to "
"nedela nic uzitecneho a mel by byt nahrazen vhodnym pouzitim "
":class:`io.TextIOWrapper` (pokud je potreba) a jeho argumentem *newline*."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2139
msgid ""
"The *parser* argument of :func:`xml.etree.ElementTree.iterparse` has been "
"deprecated, as has the *html* argument of "
":func:`~xml.etree.ElementTree.XMLParser`.  To prepare for the removal of the"
" latter, all arguments to ``XMLParser`` should be passed by keyword."
msgstr ""
"Argument *parser* funkce :func:`xml.etree.ElementTree.iterparse` byl "
"zastarale, stejne jako argument *html* "
":func:`~xml.etree.ElementTree.XMLParser`. Na pripravu odstraneni druheho, "
"wszystkie argumenty na ``XMLParser`` musi byt proseny klucovym slovem."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2146
msgid "Deprecated Features"
msgstr "Zastarale vlastnosti"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2148
msgid ""
"Running :ref:`idle` with the ``-n`` flag (no subprocess) is deprecated. "
"However, the feature will not be removed until :issue:`18823` is resolved."
msgstr ""
"Spusteni :ref:`idle` s vlajkou ``-n`` (bez podprocesu) je zastarale. "
"Vlastnost nebude vsak odstranen dokud :issue:`18823` je vyresen."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2151
msgid ""
"The site module adding a \"site-python\" directory to sys.path, if it "
"exists, is deprecated (:issue:`19375`)."
msgstr ""
"Modul site pridat \"site-python\" adresar do sys.path, pokud existuje, je "
"zastarale (:issue:`19375`)."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2157
msgid "Removed"
msgstr "Odstraneno"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2161
msgid "Operating Systems No Longer Supported"
msgstr "Operacni systemy jiz nepodporovany"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2163
msgid ""
"Support for the following operating systems has been removed from the source"
" and build tools:"
msgstr ""
"Podpora pro nasledujici operacni systemy byla odstranena ze zdrojoveho a "
"stavicich nastroju:"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2166
msgid "OS/2 (:issue:`16135`)."
msgstr "OS/2 (:issue:`16135`)."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2167
msgid "Windows 2000 (changeset e52df05b496a)."
msgstr "Windows 2000 (changeset e52df05b496a)."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2168
msgid ""
"Windows systems where ``COMSPEC`` points to ``command.com`` "
"(:issue:`14470`)."
msgstr ""
"Systemy Windows, kde ``COMSPEC`` body na ``command.com`` (:issue:`14470`)."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2169
msgid "VMS (:issue:`16136`)."
msgstr "VMS (:issue:`16136`)."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2173
msgid "API and Feature Removals"
msgstr "API a Odestrany funkci"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2175
msgid ""
"The following obsolete and previously deprecated APIs and features have been"
" removed:"
msgstr ""
"Nasledujici zastarale a drive zastarale API a vlastnosti bylo odstraneno:"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2178
msgid ""
"The unmaintained ``Misc/TextMate`` and ``Misc/vim`` directories have been "
"removed (see the `devguide <https://devguide.python.org>`_ for suggestions "
"on what to use instead)."
msgstr ""
"Nespravovane ``Misc/TextMate`` a ``Misc/vim`` adresare byly odstrany (viz "
"`devguide <https://devguide.python.org>`_ pro navrhy, co je zde pouzivat)."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2182
msgid ""
"The ``SO`` makefile macro is removed (it was replaced by the "
"``SHLIB_SUFFIX`` and ``EXT_SUFFIX`` macros) (:issue:`16754`)."
msgstr ""
"Makefile makro ``SO`` je odstraneno (bylo nahrazeno ``SHLIB_SUFFIX`` a "
"``EXT_SUFFIX`` makry) (:issue:`16754`)."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2185
msgid ""
"The ``PyThreadState.tick_counter`` field has been removed; its value has "
"been meaningless since Python 3.2, when the \"new GIL\" was introduced "
"(:issue:`19199`)."
msgstr ""
"Pole ``PyThreadState.tick_counter`` bylo odstranen; jeho hodnota byla "
"bezsmyslne od Python 3.2, kdy byl \"novy GIL\" predstavljen "
"(:issue:`19199`)."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2189
msgid ""
"``PyLoader`` and ``PyPycLoader`` have been removed from :mod:`importlib`. "
"(Contributed by Taras Lyapun in :issue:`15641`.)"
msgstr ""
"``PyLoader`` a ``PyPycLoader`` byly odstrany z :mod:`importlib`. (Prispel "
"Taras Lyapun v :issue:`15641`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2192
msgid ""
"The *strict* argument to :class:`~http.client.HTTPConnection` and "
":class:`~http.client.HTTPSConnection` has been removed.  HTTP 0.9-style "
"\"Simple Responses\" are no longer supported."
msgstr ""
"Argument *strict* na :class:`~http.client.HTTPConnection` a "
":class:`~http.client.HTTPSConnection` byl odstran. HTTP 0.9-style \"Simple "
"Responses\" jiz nejsou podporovany."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2196
msgid ""
"The deprecated :mod:`urllib.request.Request` getter and setter methods "
"``add_data``, ``has_data``, ``get_data``, ``get_type``, ``get_host``, "
"``get_selector``, ``set_proxy``, ``get_origin_req_host``, and "
"``is_unverifiable`` have been removed (use direct attribute access instead)."
msgstr ""
"Zastarale :mod:`urllib.request.Request` getter a setter metody ``add_data``,"
" ``has_data``, ``get_data``, ``get_type``, ``get_host``, ``get_selector``, "
"``set_proxy``, ``get_origin_req_host`` a ``is_unverifiable`` byly odstraneny"
" (pouzivejte pristy pristup atribut miste toho)."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2201
msgid ""
"Support for loading the deprecated ``TYPE_INT64`` has been removed from "
":mod:`marshal`.  (Contributed by Dan Riti in :issue:`15480`.)"
msgstr ""
"Podpora pro nacteni zastarale ``TYPE_INT64`` byla odstranena z "
":mod:`marshal`. (Prispel Dan Riti v :issue:`15480`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2204
msgid ""
":class:`inspect.Signature`: positional-only parameters are now required to "
"have a valid name."
msgstr ""
":class:`inspect.Signature`: pozicni-pouze parametry jsou nyní povinny mit "
"platne jmeno."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2207
msgid ""
":meth:`object.__format__` no longer accepts non-empty format strings, it now"
" raises a :exc:`TypeError` instead.  Using a non-empty string has been "
"deprecated since Python 3.2.  This change has been made to prevent a "
"situation where previously working (but incorrect) code would start failing "
"if an object gained a __format__ method, which means that your code may now "
"raise a :exc:`TypeError` if you are using an ``'s'`` format code with "
"objects that do not have a __format__ method that handles it.  See "
":issue:`7994` for background."
msgstr ""
":meth:`object.__format__` jiz neprijima neprazdne formatoř retezce, nyní "
"vyvolava :exc:`TypeError` miste. Pouzivani neprazdneho retezce bylo "
"zastarale od Python 3.2. Tato zmena byla udelana aby se zabranilo situaci, "
"kdy predtim pracu (ale nespravne) kod by zacal selhat pokud objekt ziskal "
"__format__ metodu, znamena to, ze vas kod muze nyní vyvolat :exc:`TypeError`"
" pokud pouzivate ``'s'`` kod formatu s objekty, ktere nemaji __format__ "
"metodu, ktera ji zpracovava. Viz :issue:`7994` pro pozadi."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2216
msgid ""
":meth:`!difflib.SequenceMatcher.isbjunk` and "
":meth:`!difflib.SequenceMatcher.isbpopular` were deprecated in 3.2, and have"
" now been removed: use ``x in sm.bjunk`` and ``x in sm.bpopular``, where "
"*sm* is a :class:`~difflib.SequenceMatcher` object (:issue:`13248`)."
msgstr ""
":meth:`!difflib.SequenceMatcher.isbjunk` a "
":meth:`!difflib.SequenceMatcher.isbpopular` byly zastarale v 3.2 a jsou nyní"
" odstraneny: pouzijte ``x in sm.bjunk`` a ``x in sm.bpopular``, kde *sm* je "
":class:`~difflib.SequenceMatcher` objekt (:issue:`13248`)."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2224
msgid "Code Cleanups"
msgstr "Cisteni kodu"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2226
msgid ""
"The unused and undocumented internal ``Scanner`` class has been removed from"
" the :mod:`pydoc` module."
msgstr ""
"Pouzivana a nedokumentovana vnitrni ``Scanner`` trida byla odstranena z "
"modulu :mod:`pydoc`."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2229
msgid ""
"The private and effectively unused ``_gestalt`` module has been removed, "
"along with the private :mod:`platform` functions ``_mac_ver_lookup``, "
"``_mac_ver_gstalt``, and ``_bcd2str``, which would only have ever been "
"called on badly broken OSX systems (see :issue:`18393`)."
msgstr ""
"Soukroma a efektivne nepouzivana ``_gestalt`` modul byl odstran, spolu se "
"soukromymi :mod:`platform` funkcemi ``_mac_ver_lookup``, ``_mac_ver_gstalt``"
" a ``_bcd2str``, ktere by byly volány pouze na zle rozbitych systémech OSX "
"(viz :issue:`18393`)."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2234
msgid ""
"The hardcoded copies of certain :mod:`stat` constants that were included in "
"the :mod:`tarfile` module namespace have been removed."
msgstr ""
"Pevne zapracovane kopie urcitych konstant :mod:`stat`, ktere byly zahrnuty v"
" namespace :mod:`tarfile` modulu, byly odstraneny."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2240
msgid "Porting to Python 3.4"
msgstr "Portovani na Python 3.4"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2242
msgid ""
"This section lists previously described changes and other bugfixes that may "
"require changes to your code."
msgstr ""
"Tato cast seznam drivejsicch zmenen a dalsich oprav, ktere mohou vyzidat "
"zmeny vasim kodu."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2247
msgid "Changes in 'python' Command Behavior"
msgstr "Zmeny v chovaní prikazu 'python'"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2249
msgid ""
"In a posix shell, setting the :envvar:`PATH` environment variable to an "
"empty value is equivalent to not setting it at all.  However, setting "
":envvar:`PYTHONPATH` to an empty value was *not* equivalent to not setting "
"it at all: setting :envvar:`PYTHONPATH` to an empty value was equivalent to "
"setting it to ``.``, which leads to confusion when reasoning by analogy to "
"how :envvar:`PATH` works.  The behavior now conforms to the posix convention"
" for :envvar:`PATH`."
msgstr ""
"V posix shell, nastaveni promenne oblasti :envvar:`PATH` na prazdnou hodnotu"
" je ekvivalentni s nenastavenim ji vubec. Vsak, nastaveni "
":envvar:`PYTHONPATH` na prazdnou hodnotu byl *ne* ekvivalent k nenastaveni "
"ji vubec: nastaveni :envvar:`PYTHONPATH` na prazdnou hodnotu bylo "
"ekvivalentni k nastaveni ji na ``.``, ktere vede k zmatu, kdyz se duvoda "
"analogie jak :envvar:`PATH` pracuje. Chovani se nyni shoduje s posix "
"konvenci pro :envvar:`PATH`."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2257
msgid ""
"The [X refs, Y blocks] output of a debug (``--with-pydebug``) build of the "
"CPython interpreter is now off by default.  It can be re-enabled using the "
"``-X showrefcount`` option.  (Contributed by Ezio Melotti in "
":issue:`17323`.)"
msgstr ""
"[X refs, Y blocks] vystup debug (``--with-pydebug``) stavby interpreta "
"CPython je nyní vypnuto ve vychozim. Muze byt znovu povoleno pouzitim ``-X "
"showrefcount`` moznosti. (Prispel Ezio Melotti v :issue:`17323`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2261
msgid ""
"The python command and most stdlib scripts (as well as :mod:`argparse`) now "
"output ``--version`` information to ``stdout`` instead of ``stderr`` (for "
"issue list see :ref:`other-improvements-3.4` above)."
msgstr ""
"Prikaz python a vetsina stdlib skriptu (stejne jako :mod:`argparse`) nyní "
"vystup ``--version`` informace do ``stdout`` namiste ``stderr`` (pro seznam "
"problemu viz :ref:`other-improvements-3.4` vyse)."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2267
msgid "Changes in the Python API"
msgstr "Zmeny v Python API"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2269
msgid ""
"The ABCs defined in :mod:`importlib.abc` now either raise the appropriate "
"exception or return a default value instead of raising "
":exc:`NotImplementedError` blindly. This will only affect code calling "
":func:`super` and falling through all the way to the ABCs. For "
"compatibility, catch both :exc:`NotImplementedError` or the appropriate "
"exception as needed."
msgstr ""
"ABC definovane v :mod:`importlib.abc` nyní bud vyvolaji vhodnou vyjimku nebo"
" vrati vychozi hodnotu míste slepoveho vyvolani :exc:`NotImplementedError`. "
"To ovlivni pouze kod volajici :func:`super` a propadani skrz vsechny ABCs. "
"Pro kompatibilitu, chyte obe :exc:`NotImplementedError` nebo vhodnou "
"vyjimku, jak je potreba."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2275
msgid ""
"The module type now initializes the :attr:`~module.__package__` and "
":attr:`~module.__loader__` attributes to ``None`` by default. To determine "
"if these attributes were set in a backwards-compatible fashion, use e.g. "
"``getattr(module, '__loader__', None) is not None``.  (:issue:`17115`.)"
msgstr ""
"Typ modulu nyní inicializuje atributy :attr:`~module.__package__` a "
":attr:`~module.__loader__` na ``None`` ve vychozim. K urceni, zda byly tyto "
"atributy nastaveny v zpatne-kompatibilnim způsobem, pouzijte napríklad "
"``getattr(module, '__loader__', None) is not None``. (:issue:`17115`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2281
msgid ""
":meth:`!importlib.util.module_for_loader` now sets ``__loader__`` and "
"``__package__`` unconditionally to properly support reloading. If this is "
"not desired then you will need to set these attributes manually. You can use"
" :func:`!importlib.util.module_to_load` for module management."
msgstr ""
":meth:`!importlib.util.module_for_loader` nyní nastavuje ``__loader__`` a "
"``__package__`` bez rozvahy k podpore obnovy. Pokud to neni zadouce, budete "
"muset nastavit tyto atributy rucne. Muzes pouzit "
":func:`!importlib.util.module_to_load` pro spravu modulu."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2286
msgid ""
"Import now resets relevant attributes (e.g. ``__name__``, ``__loader__``, "
"``__package__``, ``__file__``, ``__cached__``) unconditionally when "
"reloading. Note that this restores a pre-3.3 behavior in that it means a "
"module is re-found when re-loaded (:issue:`19413`)."
msgstr ""
"Import nyní resetuje prislusne atributy (napríklad ``__name__``, "
"``__loader__``, ``__package__``, ``__file__``, ``__cached__``) bez rozvahy "
"pri reloadovani. Poznamka, ze to obnovuje pre-3.3 chování, ze to znamena "
"modul je znovu nalezen, je-li obnoven (:issue:`19413`)."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2291
msgid ""
"Frozen packages no longer set ``__path__`` to a list containing the package "
"name, they now set it to an empty list.  The previous behavior could cause "
"the import system to do the wrong thing on submodule imports if there was "
"also a directory with the same name as the frozen package.  The correct way "
"to determine if a module is a package or not is to use ``hasattr(module, "
"'__path__')`` (:issue:`18065`)."
msgstr ""
"Zamrzle balicky jiz nenastavuji ``__path__`` seznamu obsahujiciho jmeno "
"balicky, nyní jej nastavuji na prazdny seznam. Predchozi chování mohlo "
"zpusobit importni system udelat spatnou vec na podmodul importy, pokud byl "
"take adresar se stejnym jmenem jako zamrzly balicky. Spravny způsob k "
"urceni, zda modul je balicky ci ne je pouziti ``hasattr(module, "
"'__path__')`` (:issue:`18065`)."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2298
msgid ""
"Frozen modules no longer define a ``__file__`` attribute. It's semantically "
"incorrect for frozen modules to set the attribute as they are not loaded "
"from any explicit location. If you must know that a module comes from frozen"
" code then you can see if the module's ``__spec__.location`` is set to "
"``'frozen'``, check if the loader is a subclass of "
":class:`importlib.machinery.FrozenImporter`, or if Python 2 compatibility is"
" necessary you can use :func:`!imp.is_frozen`."
msgstr ""
"Zamrzle moduly jiz nedefinuji atribut ``__file__``. To je semanticky "
"nespravne pro zamrzle moduly na nastaveni atributu, jak nejsou nacteny z "
"jakekoli explicitni lokace. Pokud jste se musili vedet, ze modul pochazi z "
"zamrzleho kodu, pak muzete videt, zda modul ``__spec__.location`` je "
"nastaven na ``'frozen'``, zkontrolovati, zda je loader podtrida "
":class:`importlib.machinery.FrozenImporter`, nebo pokud je kompatibilita s "
"Python 2 potreba muzes pouzit :func:`!imp.is_frozen`."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2306
msgid ""
":func:`py_compile.compile` now raises :exc:`FileExistsError` if the file "
"path it would write to is a symlink or a non-regular file. This is to act as"
" a warning that import will overwrite those files with a regular file "
"regardless of what type of file path they were originally."
msgstr ""
":func:`py_compile.compile` nyní vyvolava :exc:`FileExistsError` pokud cesta "
"souboru, kterou by psal, je symlink nebo nonregularni soubor. To je jednat "
"jako varovani, ze import prepise tyto soubory s regularni soubor bez ohledu "
"na to, jaky typ cesty souboru byli puvodne."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2311
msgid ""
":meth:`importlib.abc.SourceLoader.get_source` no longer raises "
":exc:`ImportError` when the source code being loaded triggers a "
":exc:`SyntaxError` or :exc:`UnicodeDecodeError`. As :exc:`ImportError` is "
"meant to be raised only when source code cannot be found but it should, it "
"was felt to be over-reaching/overloading of that meaning when the source "
"code is found but improperly structured. If you were catching ImportError "
"before and wish to continue to ignore syntax or decoding issues, catch all "
"three exceptions now."
msgstr ""
":meth:`importlib.abc.SourceLoader.get_source` jiz nevyvolava "
":exc:`ImportError` kdyz zdrojovy kod nacitany triggerov :exc:`SyntaxError` "
"nebo :exc:`UnicodeDecodeError`. Jak :exc:`ImportError` je zamýšlen byl "
"vyvolen pouze, kdyz zdrojovy kod nemuze byt nalezen, ale mel by byt, bylo se"
" citit na to, aby presahoval/preloadovani toho vyznam kdyz je zdrojovy kod "
"nalezen ale nepatricne strukturovany. Pokud jste byli chyceni ImportError "
"drive a vzdy se chces ignorovat syntaxi nebo dekodovani problemy, chyt nyni "
"všechny tri vyjimky."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2320
msgid ""
":func:`functools.update_wrapper` and :func:`functools.wraps` now correctly "
"set the ``__wrapped__`` attribute to the function being wrapped, even if "
"that function also had its ``__wrapped__`` attribute set. This means "
"``__wrapped__`` attributes now correctly link a stack of decorated functions"
" rather than every ``__wrapped__`` attribute in the chain referring to the "
"innermost function. Introspection libraries that assumed the previous "
"behaviour was intentional can use :func:`inspect.unwrap` to access the first"
" function in the chain that has no ``__wrapped__`` attribute."
msgstr ""
":func:`functools.update_wrapper` a :func:`functools.wraps` nyní spravne "
"nastavuji atribut ``__wrapped__`` na funkci, ktera je zabalena, i kdyz ta "
"funkce take mela sveho atributu ``__wrapped__`` nastaveno. To znamena "
"``__wrapped__`` atributy nyní spravne propojuji zasobnik ozdoben funkce nez "
"kazdy ``__wrapped__`` atribut v retezci vztahuje na nejglubssi funkci. "
"Introspekce knihovny, ktere predpokladaly, ze predchozi chování bylo zamiern"
" muze pouzit :func:`inspect.unwrap` pro pristup prvni funkci v retezci, "
"ktera nema ``__wrapped__`` atribut."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2330
msgid ""
":func:`inspect.getfullargspec` has been reimplemented on top of "
":func:`inspect.signature` and hence handles a much wider variety of callable"
" objects than it did in the past. It is expected that additional builtin and"
" extension module callables will gain signature metadata over the course of "
"the Python 3.4 series. Code that assumes that :func:`inspect.getfullargspec`"
" will fail on non-Python callables may need to be adjusted accordingly."
msgstr ""
":func:`inspect.getfullargspec` byl preimplementov na vrch "
":func:`inspect.signature` a tedy zpracovava mnohem sirsi rozsah callable "
"objektu nez v minulosti. Ocekava se, ze dalsi zavazen a rozsirovaci moduly "
"callable ziskaji podpis metadata v prubehu Python 3.4 serie. Kod, ktery "
"predpoklada, ze :func:`inspect.getfullargspec` bude selhat na non-Python "
"callable muze potrebovat byt prilagoben podle toho."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2338
msgid ""
":class:`importlib.machinery.PathFinder` now passes on the current working "
"directory to objects in :data:`sys.path_hooks` for the empty string. This "
"results in :data:`sys.path_importer_cache` never containing ``''``, thus "
"iterating through :data:`sys.path_importer_cache` based on :data:`sys.path` "
"will not find all keys. A module's ``__file__`` when imported in the current"
" working directory will also now have an absolute path, including when using"
" ``-m`` with the interpreter (except for ``__main__.__file__`` when a script"
" has been executed directly using a relative path) (Contributed by Brett "
"Cannon in :issue:`18416`).  is specified on the command-line) "
"(:issue:`18416`)."
msgstr ""
":class:`importlib.machinery.PathFinder` nyní preda aktualni pracovni adresar"
" objektu v :data:`sys.path_hooks` pro prazdny retezec. To vede k "
":data:`sys.path_importer_cache` nikdy obsahuje ``''``, tak iterovani "
":data:`sys.path_importer_cache` zalozeno na :data:`sys.path` nenajde vsechny"
" klice. Modul ``__file__`` je-li importovany v aktualni pracovni adresar "
"bude take nyní mit absolutni cestu, vcetne pri pouziti ``-m`` s interpretem "
"(krome ``__main__.__file__`` kdyz byl skript provaden primo pomoci relativni"
" cesty) (Prispel Brett Cannon v :issue:`18416`). je specifikovano na prikaz-"
"line) (:issue:`18416`)."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2349
msgid ""
"The removal of the *strict* argument to :class:`~http.client.HTTPConnection`"
" and :class:`~http.client.HTTPSConnection` changes the meaning of the "
"remaining arguments if you are specifying them positionally rather than by "
"keyword.  If you've been paying attention to deprecation warnings your code "
"should already be specifying any additional arguments via keywords."
msgstr ""
"Odstraneni *strict* argument na :class:`~http.client.HTTPConnection` a "
":class:`~http.client.HTTPSConnection` zmeni vyznam zbyvajicich argumentu, "
"pokud je specifikujete pozicne nez podle klicoveho slova. Pokud jste byli "
"venovat pozornost varovanim deprecation vas kod by jiz mel byt specifikujici"
" jakekoli dalsich argumentu prostrednictvim klice slov."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2355
msgid ""
"Strings between ``from __future__ import ...`` statements now *always* raise"
" a :exc:`SyntaxError`.  Previously if there was no leading docstring, an "
"interstitial string would sometimes be ignored.  This brings CPython into "
"compliance with the language spec; Jython and PyPy already were. "
"(:issue:`17434`)."
msgstr ""
"Retezce mezi ``from __future__ import ...`` vyrazy nyní *vzdy* vyvolaji "
":exc:`SyntaxError`. Drive, pokud zde byla zadna vede docstring, mezisoubor "
"retezec by byl niekedy ignorovan. To vede CPython do souladu se specifikaci "
"jazyka; Jython a PyPy jiz byli. (:issue:`17434`)."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2361
msgid ""
":meth:`ssl.SSLSocket.getpeercert` and :meth:`ssl.SSLSocket.do_handshake` now"
" raise an :exc:`OSError` with ``ENOTCONN`` when the ``SSLSocket`` is not "
"connected, instead of the previous behavior of raising an "
":exc:`AttributeError`.  In addition, :meth:`~ssl.SSLSocket.getpeercert` will"
" raise a :exc:`ValueError` if the handshake has not yet been done."
msgstr ""
":meth:`ssl.SSLSocket.getpeercert` a :meth:`ssl.SSLSocket.do_handshake` nyní "
"vyvolají :exc:`OSError` s ``ENOTCONN`` kdyz ``SSLSocket`` neni pripojen, "
"miste predchoziho chovani vyvolani :exc:`AttributeError`. Navic, "
":meth:`~ssl.SSLSocket.getpeercert` bude vyvolat :exc:`ValueError` pokud "
"handshake jeste nebyl proveden."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2367
msgid ""
":func:`base64.b32decode` now raises a :exc:`binascii.Error` when the input "
"string contains non-b32-alphabet characters, instead of a :exc:`TypeError`."
"  This particular :exc:`TypeError` was missed when the other "
":exc:`TypeError`\\ s were converted.  (Contributed by Serhiy Storchaka in "
":issue:`18011`.)  Note: this change was also inadvertently applied in Python"
" 3.3.3."
msgstr ""
":func:`base64.b32decode` nyní vyvolava :exc:`binascii.Error` kdyz vstupni "
"retezec obsahuje non-b32-alphabet znaky, miste :exc:`TypeError`. Tato "
"konkretni :exc:`TypeError` byla vynechana, kdyz ostatni :exc:`TypeError`\\ s"
" byly prevody. (Prispel Serhiy Storchaka v :issue:`18011`.) Poznamka: tato "
"zmena byla take nechtene aplikovana v Python 3.3.3."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2374
msgid ""
"The :attr:`!file` attribute is now automatically closed when the creating "
":class:`!cgi.FieldStorage` instance is garbage collected. If you were "
"pulling the file object out separately from the :class:`!cgi.FieldStorage` "
"instance and not keeping the instance alive, then you should either store "
"the entire :class:`!cgi.FieldStorage` instance or read the contents of the "
"file before the :class:`!cgi.FieldStorage` instance is garbage collected."
msgstr ""
"Atribut :attr:`!file` je nyní automaticky uzavren, kdyz vytvoreni "
":class:`!cgi.FieldStorage` instance je sbrany. Pokud jste byli vytahujici "
"objekt souboru zvenku z :class:`!cgi.FieldStorage` instance a nenesli "
"instance nazivu, pak byste meli bud ulozit cely :class:`!cgi.FieldStorage` "
"instance nebo cist obsah souboru pred :class:`!cgi.FieldStorage` instance je"
" sbrany."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2381
msgid ""
"Calling ``read`` or ``write`` on a closed SSL socket now raises an "
"informative :exc:`ValueError` rather than the previous more mysterious "
":exc:`AttributeError` (:issue:`9177`)."
msgstr ""
"Volani ``read`` nebo ``write`` na uzavrene SSL socket nyní vyvolava "
"informativni :exc:`ValueError` nez predchozi mysterijni "
":exc:`AttributeError` (:issue:`9177`)."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2385
msgid ""
":meth:`slice.indices` no longer produces an :exc:`OverflowError` for huge "
"values.  As a consequence of this fix, :meth:`slice.indices` now raises a "
":exc:`ValueError` if given a negative length; previously it returned "
"nonsense values (:issue:`14794`)."
msgstr ""
":meth:`slice.indices` jiz neprodukuje :exc:`OverflowError` pro obrovske "
"hodnoty. Jako dusledek teto opravy, :meth:`slice.indices` nyní vyvolava "
":exc:`ValueError` pokud je dana negativni delka; drive vracela nesmysly "
"hodnoty (:issue:`14794`)."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2390
msgid ""
"The :class:`complex` constructor, unlike the :mod:`cmath` functions, was "
"incorrectly accepting :class:`float` values if an object's ``__complex__`` "
"special method returned one.  This now raises a :exc:`TypeError`. "
"(:issue:`16290`.)"
msgstr ""
"Konstruktor :class:`complex`, na rozdil od funkci :mod:`cmath`, byl "
"nespraved prijima :class:`float` hodnoty pokud objektu ``__complex__`` "
"specialni metoda vraci jednu. To nyní vyvolava :exc:`TypeError`. "
"(:issue:`16290`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2395
msgid ""
"The :class:`int` constructor in 3.2 and 3.3 erroneously accepts "
":class:`float` values for the *base* parameter.  It is unlikely anyone was "
"doing this, but if so, it will now raise a :exc:`TypeError` "
"(:issue:`16772`)."
msgstr ""
"Konstruktor :class:`int` v 3.2 a 3.3 chybne prijimaji :class:`float` hodnoty"
" pro parametr *base*. Je malo pravdepodobne, ze nekdo udelal toto, ale pokud"
" ano, to nyní vyvolava :exc:`TypeError` (:issue:`16772`)."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2399
msgid ""
"Defaults for keyword-only arguments are now evaluated *after* defaults for "
"regular keyword arguments, instead of before.  Hopefully no one wrote any "
"code that depends on the previous buggy behavior (:issue:`16967`)."
msgstr ""
"Vychozi hodnoty pro keyword-only argumenty jsou nyní vyhodnocovany *po* "
"vychozu pro regularni keyword argumenty, nez drive. Doufejme, ze nikdo "
"nenapsal kod, ktery zavisi na predchozim buggy chovani (:issue:`16967`)."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2403
msgid ""
"Stale thread states are now cleared after :func:`~os.fork`.  This may cause "
"some system resources to be released that previously were incorrectly kept "
"perpetually alive (for example, database connections kept in thread-local "
"storage).  (:issue:`17094`.)"
msgstr ""
"Zastarale stav vlakna jsou nyní vycisteny po :func:`~os.fork`. To muze "
"zpusobit nektere systemove zdroje, ktere budou uvolneny, ktere drive byly "
"nespraved udrzovany stale zive (napriklad, databazi pripojeni udrzovane v "
"vlakno-lokalni uloziste). (:issue:`17094`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2408
msgid ""
"Parameter names in ``__annotations__`` dicts are now mangled properly, "
"similarly to :attr:`~function.__kwdefaults__`. (Contributed by Yury "
"Selivanov in :issue:`20625`.)"
msgstr ""
"Jmena parametru v ``__annotations__`` slovniky jsou nyní zmutovani spravne, "
"podobne :attr:`~function.__kwdefaults__`. (Prispel Yury Selivanov v "
":issue:`20625`.)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2412
msgid ""
":attr:`hashlib.hash.name` now always returns the identifier in lower case. "
"Previously some builtin hashes had uppercase names, but now that it is a "
"formal public interface the naming has been made consistent "
"(:issue:`18532`)."
msgstr ""
":attr:`hashlib.hash.name` nyní vzdy vraci identifikator v male pripade. "
"Drive nektere vestavene hashe meli velka jmena, ale nyní je to formalni "
"verejne rozhrani pojmenovani bylo udelano konzistentni (:issue:`18532`)."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2416
msgid ""
"Because :mod:`unittest.TestSuite` now drops references to tests after they "
"are run, test harnesses that reuse a :class:`~unittest.TestSuite` to re-run "
"a set of tests may fail.   Test suites should not be re-used in this fashion"
" since it means state is retained between test runs, breaking the test "
"isolation that :mod:`unittest` is designed to provide.  However, if the lack"
" of isolation is considered acceptable, the old behavior can be restored by "
"creating a :mod:`~unittest.TestSuite` subclass that defines a "
"``_removeTestAtIndex`` method that does nothing (see "
":meth:`.TestSuite.__iter__`) (:issue:`11798`)."
msgstr ""
"Protoze :mod:`unittest.TestSuite` nyní pusti odkazy na testy po jejich "
"spusteni, test harnesy, ktere znovupouzivaji :class:`~unittest.TestSuite` "
"znovu-spustit sadu testu mohou selhat. Sady testu by nemely byt "
"znovupouzivany toto modo, coz znamena stat je zachovana mezi test zbrusu, "
"brakovina test izolace, kterou :mod:`unittest` je navrzena poskytnout. Vsak,"
" pokud se nedostatek izolace povazuje za prijateln, stary chov muze byt "
"obnoven vytvorenim :mod:`~unittest.TestSuite` podtridy, ktera definuje "
"``_removeTestAtIndex`` metodu, ktera nedela nic (viz "
":meth:`.TestSuite.__iter__`) (:issue:`11798`)."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2426
msgid ""
":mod:`unittest` now uses :mod:`argparse` for command line parsing.  There "
"are certain invalid command forms that used to work that are no longer "
"allowed; in theory this should not cause backward compatibility issues since"
" the disallowed command forms didn't make any sense and are unlikely to be "
"in use."
msgstr ""
":mod:`unittest` nyní pouziva :mod:`argparse` pro prikazovey parsing. "
"Existuji urcite nevyznamne prikazovye tvary, ktere byli pouzity, ktere jiz "
"nejsou povoleny; v teorii to by nemelo zpusobit zpatne problemy "
"kompatibility, coz proto, ze zakazane tvary prikazu nedavaly smysl a je malo"
" pravdepodobne, ze je budete pouzivat."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2431
msgid ""
"The :func:`re.split`, :func:`re.findall`, and :func:`re.sub` functions, and "
"the :meth:`~re.Match.group` and :meth:`~re.Match.groups` methods of "
"``match`` objects now always return a *bytes* object when the string to be "
"matched is a :term:`bytes-like object`.  Previously the return type matched "
"the input type, so if your code was depending on the return value being, "
"say, a ``bytearray``, you will need to change your code."
msgstr ""
"Funkce :func:`re.split`, :func:`re.findall` a :func:`re.sub` a metody "
":meth:`~re.Match.group` a :meth:`~re.Match.groups` objektu ``match`` nyní "
"vzdy vracejici *bytes* objekt kdyz je retezec, ktery ma byt spatovany je "
":term:`bytes-like object`. Drive typ vraceni shodne vstupni typ, takze pokud"
" vas kod byl zavisejici na vrati se hodnota byt, napriklad ``bytearray``, "
"budete muset zmenit vas kod."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2438
msgid ""
":mod:`!audioop` functions now raise an error immediately if passed string "
"input, instead of failing randomly later on (:issue:`16685`)."
msgstr ""
"Funkce :mod:`!audioop` nyní vyvolaji chybu hned, pokud predane vstupni "
"retezec, miste se nizko selhat pozdeji (:issue:`16685`)."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2441
msgid ""
"The new *convert_charrefs* argument to :class:`~html.parser.HTMLParser` "
"currently defaults to ``False`` for backward compatibility, but will "
"eventually be changed to default to ``True``.  It is recommended that you "
"add this keyword, with the appropriate value, to any "
":class:`~html.parser.HTMLParser` calls in your code (:issue:`13633`)."
msgstr ""
"Novy argument *convert_charrefs* na :class:`~html.parser.HTMLParser` nyní "
"vychozi na ``False`` pro zpetné kompatibility, ale bude nakonec zmenen na "
"vychozi na ``True``. Je doporuceno, ze jste pridan tyto klice slova, s "
"vhodnou hodnotu, na jakekoli :class:`~html.parser.HTMLParser` volani v vase "
"kodu (:issue:`13633`)."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2447
msgid ""
"Since the *digestmod* argument to the :func:`hmac.new` function will in the "
"future have no default, all calls to :func:`hmac.new` should be changed to "
"explicitly specify a *digestmod* (:issue:`17276`)."
msgstr ""
"Vzhledem k tomu, ze *digestmod* argument na funkci :func:`hmac.new` bude v "
"budoucnosti nema vychozi, vse volani na :func:`hmac.new` by mela byt zmenen "
"na explicitne specifikovat *digestmod* (:issue:`17276`)."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2451
msgid ""
"Calling :func:`sysconfig.get_config_var` with the ``SO`` key, or looking "
"``SO`` up in the results of a call to :func:`sysconfig.get_config_vars` is "
"deprecated.  This key should be replaced by ``EXT_SUFFIX`` or "
"``SHLIB_SUFFIX``, depending on the context (:issue:`19555`)."
msgstr ""
"Volani :func:`sysconfig.get_config_var` s ``SO`` klicem, nebo hledani ``SO``"
" do vysledku vola na :func:`sysconfig.get_config_vars` je zastarale. Tento "
"klic by mel byt nahrazen ``EXT_SUFFIX`` nebo ``SHLIB_SUFFIX``, v zavislosti "
"na kontextu (:issue:`19555`)."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2456
msgid ""
"Any calls to ``open`` functions that specify ``U`` should be modified. ``U``"
" is ineffective in Python3 and will eventually raise an error if used. "
"Depending on the function, the equivalent of its old Python2 behavior can be"
" achieved using either a *newline* argument, or if necessary by wrapping the"
" stream in :mod:`~io.TextIOWrapper` to use its *newline* argument "
"(:issue:`15204`)."
msgstr ""
"Jake volani na ``open`` funkce, ktere specifikuji ``U`` by mely byt "
"upraveny. ``U`` je necinny v Python3 a bude nakonec vyhodit chybu, pokud je "
"pouzit. Vzhledem k funkci, ekvivalent jeho stareho Python2 chov muze byt "
"dosazeno pouzitim bud *newline* argument, nebo v pripade potreby obalen "
"proud v :mod:`~io.TextIOWrapper` pouzivat jeho argument *newline* "
"(:issue:`15204`)."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2463
msgid ""
"If you use ``pyvenv`` in a script and desire that pip *not* be installed, "
"you must add ``--without-pip`` to your command invocation."
msgstr ""
"Pokud pouzivate ``pyvenv`` v skriptu a pozadovat, aby pip *ne* byl "
"instalovan, musim pridat ``--without-pip`` na vas prikaz vyvolan."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2467
msgid ""
"The default behavior of :func:`json.dump` and :func:`json.dumps` when an "
"indent is specified has changed: it no longer produces trailing spaces after"
" the item separating commas at the ends of lines.  This will matter only if "
"you have tests that are doing white-space-sensitive comparisons of such "
"output (:issue:`16333`)."
msgstr ""
"Vychozi chov :func:`json.dump` a :func:`json.dumps` kdyz indent je "
"specifikovany se zmena: jiz neprodukuje koncove prostory po oddelijici "
"carkach na koncich radku. To bude zalozit pouze pokud mate testy, ktere jsou"
" provadejici bily prostor-sensitive srovnani takoveho vystupu "
"(:issue:`16333`)."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2473
msgid ""
":mod:`doctest` now looks for doctests in extension module ``__doc__`` "
"strings, so if your doctest test discovery includes extension modules that "
"have things that look like doctests in them you may see test failures you've"
" never seen before when running your tests (:issue:`3158`)."
msgstr ""
":mod:`doctest` nyní hleda doctesty v rozsirovaci modul ``__doc__`` retezci, "
"takze pokud vas doctest test objevovani zahrnuje rozsirovaci moduly, ktere "
"maji veci, ktere vypadaji jako doctesty v nich mohou videt selhani testu, "
"ktere jste nikdy videli drive, kdyz spustite sve testy (:issue:`3158`)."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2478
msgid ""
"The :mod:`collections.abc` module has been slightly refactored as part of "
"the Python startup improvements.  As a consequence of this, it is no longer "
"the case that importing :mod:`collections` automatically imports "
":mod:`collections.abc`.  If your program depended on the (undocumented) "
"implicit import, you will need to add an explicit ``import collections.abc``"
" (:issue:`20784`)."
msgstr ""
"Modul :mod:`collections.abc` byl jemne prestrukturovan jako soucas Python "
"startup zlepseni. Jako dusledek toto, jiz neni pripad, ze import "
":mod:`collections` automaticky importy :mod:`collections.abc`. Pokud vas "
"program zavisejici na (nedokumentovany) implicitni import, budete muset "
"pridat explicitni ``import collections.abc`` (:issue:`20784`)."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2487
msgid "Changes in the C API"
msgstr "Zmeny v C API"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2489
msgid ""
":c:func:`PyEval_EvalFrameEx`, :c:func:`PyObject_Repr`, and "
":c:func:`PyObject_Str`, along with some other internal C APIs, now include a"
" debugging assertion that ensures they are not used in situations where they"
" may silently discard a currently active exception. In cases where "
"discarding the active exception is expected and desired (for example, "
"because it has already been saved locally with :c:func:`PyErr_Fetch` or is "
"being deliberately replaced with a different exception), an explicit "
":c:func:`PyErr_Clear` call will be needed to avoid triggering the assertion "
"when invoking these operations (directly or indirectly) and running against "
"a version of Python that is compiled with assertions enabled."
msgstr ""
":c:func:`PyEval_EvalFrameEx`, :c:func:`PyObject_Repr` a "
":c:func:`PyObject_Str`, spolu s nekteryma jinymi vnitrnim C APIs, nyní "
"zahrnout ladicim utrzen, ktery zajistuje, ze se nesleduji v situacich, kde "
"mohou tiche zahodit aktivni vyjimku. V pripade, kde zahotovani aktivni "
"vyjimka je ocekavany a pozadovany (napríklad, protoze byl jiz ulozven "
"lokalne s :c:func:`PyErr_Fetch` nebo je byl zamiern nahrazen jinou "
"vyjimkou), explicitni :c:func:`PyErr_Clear` volani bude potreba, aby se "
"zabranilo spusteni utrzen, kdyz se vyvolaji tyto operace (primo nebo "
"neprime) a spusteni proti verzi Python, ktery je zkompilov s utrzen "
"povoleno."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2501
msgid ""
":c:func:`PyErr_SetImportError` now sets :exc:`TypeError` when its **msg** "
"argument is not set. Previously only ``NULL`` was returned with no exception"
" set."
msgstr ""
":c:func:`PyErr_SetImportError` nyní sady :exc:`TypeError` kdyz je jeho "
"**msg** argument neni nastaven. Drive pouze ``NULL`` byl vracia bez vyjimky "
"nastaven."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2505
msgid ""
"The result of the :c:data:`PyOS_ReadlineFunctionPointer` callback must now "
"be a string allocated by :c:func:`PyMem_RawMalloc` or "
":c:func:`PyMem_RawRealloc`, or ``NULL`` if an error occurred, instead of a "
"string allocated by :c:func:`PyMem_Malloc` or :c:func:`PyMem_Realloc` "
"(:issue:`16742`)"
msgstr ""
"Vysledek zpetneho volani :c:data:`PyOS_ReadlineFunctionPointer` nyni musi "
"byt retezec alokovany :c:func:`PyMem_RawMalloc` nebo "
":c:func:`PyMem_RawRealloc` nebo ``NULL`` pokud doslo k chybe, miste retezce "
"alokovany :c:func:`PyMem_Malloc` nebo :c:func:`PyMem_Realloc` "
"(:issue:`16742`)"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2511
msgid ""
":c:func:`PyThread_set_key_value` now always set the value. In Python 3.3, "
"the function did nothing if the key already exists (if the current value is "
"a non-``NULL`` pointer)."
msgstr ""
":c:func:`PyThread_set_key_value` nyní vzdy nastavi hodnotu. V Python 3.3, "
"funkce nedela nic pokud klic jiz existuje (pokud je aktualni hodnota "
"non-``NULL`` ukazatel)."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2515
msgid ""
"The ``f_tstate`` (thread state) field of the :c:type:`PyFrameObject` "
"structure has been removed to fix a bug: see :issue:`14432` for the "
"rationale."
msgstr ""
"Pole ``f_tstate`` (vlakno stav) :c:type:`PyFrameObject` struktura bylo "
"odstranen opravit chybu: viz :issue:`14432` pro duvodovost."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2520
msgid "Changed in 3.4.3"
msgstr "Zmeny v 3.4.3"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2525
msgid ""
"PEP 476: Enabling certificate verification by default for stdlib http "
"clients"
msgstr ""
"PEP 476: Povoleni verifikace certifikatu ve vychozim pro stdlib http "
"klientem"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2527
msgid ""
":mod:`http.client` and modules which use it, such as :mod:`urllib.request` "
"and :mod:`xmlrpc.client`, will now verify that the server presents a "
"certificate which is signed by a CA in the platform trust store and whose "
"hostname matches the hostname being requested by default, significantly "
"improving security for many applications."
msgstr ""
":mod:`http.client` a moduly, ktere ji pouzivaji, jako :mod:`urllib.request` "
"a :mod:`xmlrpc.client`, bude nyni overit, ze server prezentuje certifikat, "
"ktery je podepsan CA v platforme spolehlivost uloziste a jehoz hostname "
"odpovida hostname jsou pozadavky ve vychozim, vyznamne zlepseni zabezpeceni "
"mnoho aplikaci."

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2533
msgid ""
"For applications which require the old previous behavior, they can pass an "
"alternate context::"
msgstr ""
"Pro aplikace, ktere vyziduji stary predchozi chov, mohou projit alternativni"
" kontext::"

#: ../../whatsnew/3.4.rst:2536
msgid ""
"import urllib.request\n"
"import ssl\n"
"\n"
"# This disables all verification\n"
"context = ssl._create_unverified_context()\n"
"\n"
"# This allows using a specific certificate for the host, which doesn't need\n"
"# to be in the trust store\n"
"context = ssl.create_default_context(cafile=\"/path/to/file.crt\")\n"
"\n"
"urllib.request.urlopen(\"https://invalid-cert\", context=context)"
msgstr ""
"import urllib.request\n"
"import ssl\n"
"\n"
"# Toto zakaze vsechny verifikace\n"
"context = ssl._create_unverified_context()\n"
"\n"
"# Toto umoznuje pouziti konkretni certifikat pro gospodarstvi, ktere neni potreba\n"
"# byt v ulozisti spolehlivosti\n"
"context = ssl.create_default_context(cafile=\"/path/to/file.crt\")\n"
"\n"
"urllib.request.urlopen(\"https://invalid-cert\", context=context)"

